{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns","id":1249810,"title":"Werewolf 5th concerns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-29T15:48:52-07:00","id":1249810,"title":"Werewolf 5th concerns","content":"Reposting this link cause great points and he's more qualified than myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0tUL6VtKFxc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0tUL6VtKFxc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0tUL6VtKFxc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/0tUL6VtKFxc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If werewolf the Apocalypse fifth edition becomes a possibility, I don't want werewolf to go where vampire went. For a lot of reasons <br /> <br /> 1. It's viseral. It helps with the gravitas of not only my actions, but other players and villains.<br /> 2. Werewolf thrives on conflict. Physical and mental. Your a dangerous beast who can kill at a drop of a hat. Cite, Wolf man, werewolf of London, skinwalkers.<br /> 3. shapeshifters are the original body horror. Your body warping and contorting to reshape your flesh.<br /> 4. The topics that would be cringing. I play werewolf to do those feats that I as me normally wouldn't be able to do or have the abilities to serve Gaia that doesn't involve annoying my senators every so often.<br /> 5. I really don't want the tribes redesigned to fit the social justus warrior narrative. Not only it's been taken care of, but like any wolf pack, there are alphas and omegas, on pack and tribal level. If pack Dynamics get tweaked to fit the new discoveries with wolf social structure then go for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Got a few more but it'll sound like I'm repeating the same points. In the age of outrage and the golden hair, I want my games focused on the real matters at hand. Like any good werewolf movie, it shouldn't be soft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T21:36:04-07:00","id":1249878,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 5th edition has already been mentioned - White Wolf are working on it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't take a mind to that ranting on the link provided though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T01:21:38-07:00","id":1249902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns#post1249810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reposting this link cause great points and he's more qualified than myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want my 20 minutes back personally. &quot;I hate SJWs, so V5 sucks,&quot; isn't a great point and... yeah, that's about all that was said in those 20 minutes. I'm not a fan of V5. I do not like V5's direction and what it implies for W5... but there's actual good points to make about that, none of which are present in this nonsense video.<br /> <br /> You list also seems well... divorced from what's in V5 and WtA already anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T02:39:09-07:00","id":1249911,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned werewolf was always a game about (pardon me for using the term) Social Justice Warrior.<br /> WtA has never been a game about &quot;killing things&quot;, It is a game about saving the planet from its excess.<br /> One of the underlying themes of werewolf revised was that if fera had spent more time &quot;annoying their senators&quot; than slashing casually at things the overall situation would be better.<br /> <br /> Besides the tribes have always been about various kind of &quot;SWJ&quot; (again sorry for the term, I really think it's terrible)<br /> <br /> Wendigo with their problems with White colonialism, or the Children of Gaia, or the Furies who fought sexism and patriarchy, or the hyper-primitivist Red Talons, or against the bone gnawers Who lived in the lowest strata of society...in any case I think everything it's already there.<br /> <br /> Even the &quot;werewolves thrives on conflict&quot; it's wrong.<br /> <br /> The book are incredibly clear that conflict is killing the fera. Since the war of rage.<br /> The eternal conflict is not making the garou stronger, it's weakening them generation after generation.<br /> <br /> Even more, by embracing conflict blindly werewolves embrace the wyrm. There are reason if wisdom should go side by side with honor and valor.<br /> <br /> If you kill a pentex employee, maybe you will weaken pentex, but you will empower the urge wyrms in Malfeas.<br /> <br /> It is an underlying theme in the world or Darkness: the splats are blinded and distracted by trivial things that keep them from the important things. The blinding thing can varies, It can be Ascension War for mages, the jhyad for Vampires, or the internal conflicts of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> The Tribes are not stronger because Konietzko and Albrecht are at each other's throtat. Eternal strife just helps the wyrm.<br /> <br /> Just think about the story of the White Howlers. It's a giant metaphor of what is wrong with werewolves. You can't just throw yourself at the wyrm, Klaive in hands,fangs first. If you attack without wisdome, if you live just by rage, you are walking the spyral of the wyrm. The Howlers went on and one down the spyral, fighting at every level with even more rage. End in the end they were the Howlers no more, but the Black Spyral Dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2018, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T02:56:49-07:00","id":1249914,"title":"","content":"Werewolves and Mummies are &quot;SJWs&quot; kind of by definition. Well they're not all warriors. You have your rogues, paladins, priests...<br /> <br /> I mean how could a game about the earth fighting back against humanity's worst excesses NOT be political and progressive? With that said, Werewolves are incredibly conservative on many social issues (the Litany springs to mind) and so it's in a similar position to Mage. It has Conservative (My Mage thinks the world was perfect before X and wants to go back to it) and Liberal elements (the world will be perfect when we Y), which seems to only upset conservative types in my experience, who complain endlessly about M20 being SJW nonsense or something like that. Who would have thought that a game about people wanting to change the world for the better might end up having diverse political elements.<br /> <br /> I'm going to try and resist an urge to threadcap, but it's hard to see &quot;I believe this game about supernatural (anti)heroes saving the world from corrupt corporations and pollution (and sometimes protecting the rights of marginalized groups like Aboriginals and the First Nations) and fighting a spiritual manifestation of greed and malice is going to become too socially progressive for my liking.&quot; and not make fun of it a *little* bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-30-2018, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T03:52:13-07:00","id":1249922,"title":"","content":"Rewriting the Tribes to fit them in social nowdays clothes would be in my opinion the big mistake. Very big mistake. They are conservative. Right. Would Red Talons change? Yes they could be more radical. Would Glass Walkers change? they would be more in Weaver grip cause of overwhelming tech life (the Weaver is winning the war isn't she, twit, face and inst made the peoples living drones, Wyrm is one step after her, and Wyld just try to defend himself like always but much more violent) ... I could write about every tribe but it's not necessary, <br /> <br /> Werewolf is conflict game. WW already redesigned game logo with big WAR glyph, so it might mean that it's all out conflict. I see tribes more pissed and agresive. Don't know about the totems. I would like to see the game more ,,sharp&quot; - we against them. We against everyone who's trying to step on our sacret grounds. How the new inquisition would chase the ,,ghosts&quot; ? Yes, Vampires are in real problem, but garou can always step side to Umbra and strike like ghosts they partly are.<br /> <br /> Am I affraid about Werewolf 5th? Yes and no. If Gentelman Gamer would be leader of this project I (after W20 Book of Wyrm) am confident about his ideas and skills and it might be very good game. <br /> <br /> I am afraid that they would put all the garou tribes in LGBT frames cause it's trendy nowdays. I wish a raw pure adrenaline game. But it's only my wishlist and nothing more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:11:14-07:00","id":1249924,"title":"","content":"Considering that LGBT people make up a significant percentage of the population, including them in tabletop games isn't a political move. It's apolitical.<br /> <br /> Excluding LGBT people, however, can be a political move on the part of developers.<br /> <br /> &quot;LGBT inclusion is just trendy&quot; unknowlingly means, in many cases, &quot;this is new and confusing to me and is probably being included to make me uncomfortable.&quot; It's not that any of this is new (I can show you cultures that have existed for thousands of years with a &quot;third gender&quot;, and examples of publicly accepted homosexual romance/lust in ancient civilizations like Rome and Athens and Sparta), it's that it *feels* new because more people can be more honest about who they are and don't feel the need to hide it. No one is going to apologize if it upsets you.<br /> <br /> All it takes is a sidebar explaining that the Furies accept non-binary and trans women into their ranks (perhaps with some of their Elders being very conservative on the issue and only wanting &quot;women born women&quot; among them). That won't turn Werewolf into a Lesbian Feelings Simulator; these Furies would still be tearing banes and fomori apart, the table would just feel more inclusive to certain people who want to play. It can be an action-fueled murder-fest and also be inclusive and positive. And do the Litany's demands that Garou don't lay with other Garou apply to same-sex couples? These are issues which would be very important to a lot of people in the Garou Nation. Greek armies sometimes paired young men together and encouraged them to fall in love (either platonically or romantically) so that they would fight well to protect eachother, watch eachother's backs. I bring this up because it shows that you can tell a story about homoeroticism which is still incredibly violent and action-driven.<br /> <br /> Speaking of LGBT stuff, can someone remind me if anyone other than the Ananasi can learn that Gift where they become the opposite sex? Obviously most use it for disguise or seduction (and in extreme cases for fertility), but there's definitely room for someone to play a Loki style character who flips between man and woman depending on the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-30-2018, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:22:34-07:00","id":1249928,"title":"","content":"Indeed, in ancient greece the Theban Sacred Band (300 warriors, 150 couples) was the most elite unit in Greece. So incredible it was that the Sacred Band destroyed the Spartiates at Leuttra, and at the time Spartiates were known to had no rival in open field battles.<br /> After Leuttra the Band was undefeated for 30 years, and perished only when it met Alexander in the field.<br /> <br /> So getting homosexuals in the tribes really doens't diminish the &quot;action-drive&quot; of the setting, it just allows more people to play freely the game.<br /> Besides, I do not really recall &quot;homophobia&quot; as one of the core theme of Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2018, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:31:05-07:00","id":1249930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249928#post1249928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, in ancient greece the Theban Sacred Band was the most elite unit in Greece. So incredible it was that the Sacred Band destroyed the Spartiates at Leuttra, and at the time Spartiates were known to had no rival in open field battles.<br /> After Leuttra the Band was undefeated for 30 years, and perished only when it met Alexander in the field.<br /> <br /> So getting homosexuals in the tribes really doens't diminish the &quot;action-drive&quot; of the setting, it just allows more people to play freely the game.<br /> Besides, I do not really recall &quot;homophobia&quot; as one of the core theme of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, the Thebans were the ones who had orgies and got annoyed when people tried to bring girls right? EDIT: Not the sacred band of thebes, a random ancient greek anecdote.<br /> <br /> And the Spartans were incredibly fierce at that time. A hundred years later they were dying out due to inbreeding; they had a dumb law about only the child of two spartans being a spartan, and deaths from disease and war meant they were marrying cousins and sisters (and sleeping with foreigners, male and female, for fun) as the gene pool narrowed. It didn't help that their education system killed a bunch of boys (they would starve them and make them fight eachother), and that they left any child who &quot;seemed sickly&quot; out in the woods. Spartans are a perfect example of the worst impulses of the Garou nation in an actual civilization, which is quite interesting. So much devotion to strength that they made themselves weak.<br /> <br /> Athens succeeded because unlike Sparta their horniness wasn't purely directed inward. A lot like the Garou going around sowing wild oats to continue the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-30-2018, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:47:06-07:00","id":1249932,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be werewolf the Apocalypse if I have to check in or stop if a player doesn't feel comfortable when I approach certain topics. The story can't progress if they would rather respond to flight than fight out of character. The new comfort zone system could be easily exploited, from uncomfortable topics, unfriendly words in or out of character, to the levels of Gore that the game can generate. Also the refusal to discuss what's making a player uncomfortable would halt or end a story. It's not productive, fade to Black should only be used as cliff hangers, and nothing ventured is nothing gained.<br /> <br /> Sexual identity (not to be confused with gender) was already taken care of in rage across the world 20. The litany say garou shall not lay with garou, it doesnt say what gender. Heading that off at the pass. Me personally I don't care what orientation they are in or out of character, as long as their characters abide by the litany, they can do whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:50:07-07:00","id":1249935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249914#post1249914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to try and resist an urge to threadcap, but it's hard to see &quot;I believe this game about supernatural (anti)heroes saving the world from corrupt corporations and pollution (and sometimes protecting the rights of marginalized groups like Aboriginals and the First Nations) and fighting a spiritual manifestation of greed and malice is going to become too socially progressive for my liking.&quot; and not make fun of it a *little* bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially, since that has been the game from its very inception. For all the Captain Planet jibes against WtA, at least it has never stopped outright acknowledging that stuff needs to be done and there is no magic bullet to fix the world or its issues. One of my favourite things about it HAS been that the struggle with the american tribes is REALLY complicated and no true fix can be ever found for it without some huge introspection by Fianna, Silver Fangs, Fenrir and Children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> <br /> To the LTGBA+ and WtA thing, I have to admit that Chaging Ways' Metis section pretty much did that wrong. The constant &quot;But look, they are gay,TOO&quot; in the most childish way really grinded on me, and I wanted there to be a blatant 'Yes, garou are more tolerant of homosexuality' message in the book. THAT is what I fear for W5 over what the video says, poorly executed concepts that are surface level and don't really go into the meat of the issue.<br /> <br /> That, and the Wendigo section in that chapter is horrid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T04:55:14-07:00","id":1249936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249932#post1249932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be werewolf the Apocalypse if I have to check in or stop if a player doesn't feel comfortable when I approach certain topics. The story can't progress if they would rather respond to flight than fight out of character. The new comfort zone system could be easily exploited, from uncomfortable topics, unfriendly words in or out of character, to the levels of Gore that the game can generate. Also the refusal to discuss what's making a player uncomfortable would halt or end a story. It's not productive, fade to Black should only be used as cliff hangers, and nothing ventured is nothing gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>A player who doesn't want to explore the concepts found in WtA won't join a WtA game. If they are asking you to not deal with certain topics, there is a very good reason for that. You don't know their history or reasons why they feel they cannot deal with subjects in a safe setting, but you should respect that they are brave enough to speak about it.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying is meant to be fun for everyone, dredging up old traumas is the polar opposite of fun for people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T05:05:24-07:00","id":1249937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249936#post1249936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A player who doesn't want to explore the concepts found in WtA won't join a WtA game. If they are asking you to not deal with certain topics, there is a very good reason for that. You don't know their history or reasons why they feel they cannot deal with subjects in a safe setting, but you should respect that they are brave enough to speak about it.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying is meant to be fun for everyone, dredging up old traumas is the polar opposite of fun for people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean we've slipped from &quot;I don't want it to be LGBT trendy SJW stuff&quot; to &quot;I don't want to have to consider the wellbeing of my players&quot;, this is starting to feel like quite the downward spiral (if you'll pardon the allusion).<br /> <br /> I mean I include some really horrible stuff when I run VtM and MtA, and the only WtA game I have planned for the future is one which ends with the New Wyrm and Ananasa (The New Weaver) murdering all of the player characters with a swarm of Ananasi Metis and wyrmish spirits as a bittersweet reward for helping them replace the corrupted members of the triat, since they've discovered too much and could threaten balance in the future with what they've learned. With that said, I play things by ear and I don't push too hard. One of my players lost a friend to suicide, so when I did the session 0 of my Vampire game I asked her if she would struggle to deal with stuff relating to that; as it turns out she was fine and it worked out, but if she had been in a worse place and I hadn't asked it could have led to a huge falling out at the table which would have been my fault.<br /> <br /> So none of the themes or high action need to be discarded, STs just need to think about their players a bit more and be generally inclusive. None of this will distract from what WtA is about. You can exclude the rapist fomori who murders people with their genitals or bodily fluids if one of the players would find it upsetting or if it felt wrong for the table, and you can always replace it with something that achieves the same effect (a brain eater or a fomorus which spreads a horrific mental illness). And having LGBT werewolves among the PCs won't distract from any of this either. In my game some of the NPCs are gay, including a major antagonist and several of their allies, and it's just a backdrop that effects the social side of the game and alters the prospects of the PCs if any of them want to romance anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-30-2018, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T05:08:55-07:00","id":1249938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249932#post1249932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be werewolf the Apocalypse if I have to check in or stop if a player doesn't feel comfortable when I approach certain topics. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And yet Werewolf just tells you to do just that: checking if the player is comfortable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Page 340 of W20 Corebook<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>GOING TOO FAR</i><br /> <i>Horror-based roleplaying games involve consensual exploration of personal and social taboos; pushing limits is part of their appeal. Even in a horror-based game, though, there still are limits. Those boundaries depend upon the player\u2019s tastes, the relationships between those players, the life-experiences they\u2019ve had, the degree to which they trust each other, and the point at which their feelings tilt from enjoyment to alarm. We can\u2019t tell you where those limits are in your particular group, but we can tell you this: Push too far, and you can hurt feelings, wreck friendships, and destroy the gaming group itself.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Generally, it\u2019s a good idea to be careful with hotbutton topics. Politics and religion may or may not be fair game, depending on your group. Be very wary of using rape, torture, molestation, domestic violence, or child abuse unless you already have a good sense of your friends\u2019 emotional triggers and the signs they display when someone\u2019s approaching those limits. Even then, we recommend an out-of-game discussion or two about story elements that might trip a player\u2019s trigger\u2026 conducted before that story element comes into play. If a player indicates that such-and-such is</i><br /> <i>a hot topic, don\u2019t go there; even if he doesn\u2019t say as much, avoid topics or descriptions that you know, from experience, might seem too sensitive to touch.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Taking a page from the BDSM playbook, you might want to offer a safeword for use within your group. If a player starts to feel uncomfortable, he or she can simply use a prearranged phrase or gesture to say, That\u2019s enough. Stop. In that case, all parties are responsible for maintaining limits; the players must assert them, and the Storyteller(s) must respect them. People don\u2019t always recognize their own emotional triggers until after someone\u2019s hit one. For that reason (among others), keep a watchful eye on your players when you start to move into potentially explosive</i><br /> <i>territory. If one friend tenses at your elaborate description of crucified babies, back off and perhaps \u201cfade to black.\u201d A fade-out beats an argument or tears. If or when you do hit emotional land mines, don\u2019t fight for your right to hurt people. Back off, apologize, and maybe call a break while things get sorted out.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Yeah, Werewolf is a horror game, but the \u201cgame\u201d part comes before the \u201chorror\u201d part. If someone feels traumatized for real, the game\u2019s no longer fun.</i><br /> <br /> <i>.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> So yeah, you can play Werewolf the Apocalypse while checking if players are in or out their comfort-zone. I'll say even more: you can't play Werewolf without doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2018, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T05:12:54-07:00","id":1249939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249938#post1249938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 340 of W20 Corebook<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">GOING TOO FAR<br /> <br /> Horror-based roleplaying games involve consensual exploration of personal and social taboos; pushing limits is part of their appeal. Even in a horror-based game, though, there still are limits. Those boundaries depend upon the player\u2019s tastes, the relationships between those players, the life-experiences they\u2019ve had, the degree to which they trust each other, and the point at which their feelings tilt from enjoyment to alarm. We can\u2019t tell you where those limits are in your particular group, but we can tell you this: Push too far, and you can hurt feelings, wreck friendships, and destroy the gaming group itself.<br /> <br /> Generally, it\u2019s a good idea to be careful with hotbutton topics. Politics and religion may or may not be fair game, depending on your group. Be very wary of using rape, torture, molestation, domestic violence, or child abuse unless you already have a good sense of your friends\u2019 emotional triggers and the signs they display when someone\u2019s approaching those limits. Even then, we recommend an out-of-game discussion or two about story elements that might trip a player\u2019s trigger\u2026 conducted before that story element comes into play. If a player indicates that such-and-such is a hot topic, don\u2019t go there; even if he doesn\u2019t say as much, avoid topics or descriptions that you know, from experience, might seem too sensitive to touch.<br /> <br /> Taking a page from the BDSM playbook, you might want to offer a safeword for use within your group. If a player starts to feel uncomfortable, he or she can simply use a prearranged phrase or gesture to say, That\u2019s enough. Stop. In that case, all parties are responsible for maintaining limits; the players must assert them, and the Storyteller(s) must respect them. People don\u2019t always recognize their own emotional triggers until after someone\u2019s hit one. For that reason (among others), keep a watchful eye on your players when you start to move into potentially explosive<br /> territory. If one friend tenses at your elaborate description of crucified babies, back off and perhaps \u201cfade to black.\u201d A fade-out beats an argument or tears. If or when you do hit emotional land mines, don\u2019t fight for your right to hurt people. Back off, apologize, and maybe call a break while things get sorted out.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Werewolf is a horror game, but the \u201cgame\u201d part comes before the \u201chorror\u201d part. If someone feels traumatized for real, the game\u2019s no longer fun.</span><br /> <br /> So yeah, you can play Werewolf the Apocalypse while checking if players are in or out their comfort-zone. I'll say even more: you can't play Werewolf without doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agreed with this. And this is all the more important *because* Werewolf is a horror game. Good horror is, at the end of the day, enjoyable. Even if it's deeply discomforting or gives you some nightmares, horror can be really powerful and worthwhile if it's done well. And having villains who do truly disgusting things makes it more cathartic when you tear them apart, and more terrifying when they defeat you. It helps you to feel like more of a hero. But all of that comes with the caveat of respecting your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T06:17:25-07:00","id":1249944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249928#post1249928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, in ancient greece the Theban Sacred Band (300 warriors, 150 couples) was the most elite unit in Greece. So incredible it was that the Sacred Band destroyed the Spartiates at Leuttra, and at the time Spartiates were known to had no rival in open field battles.<br /> After Leuttra the Band was undefeated for 30 years, and perished only when it met Alexander in the field.</div> </div> </div> </div> As a curiosity, it was actually Philippos, Alexander's father.<br /> At Chaeronea they refused to surrender even after all their allies fled the battle and even if Philippos had tried to negotiate, suggesting to let them go away with all their armors, weapons and fallen comrades. To no avail, apparently, as the Band was firm in not retreating from a battlefield where their friends and lovers had shed their blood.<br /> And when the last member of the Sacred Band was put down, apparently Philippos seeing they were all fallen fighting, no one ran away, declared &quot;Perish any man who suspects that these men either did or suffered anything unseemly.&quot;<br /> or, as some more cynical viewers think, he just threatened of death penalty any of his soldiers or allies that would have dared to desecrate their corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T07:05:01-07:00","id":1249955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249911#post1249911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm concerned werewolf was always a game about (pardon me for using the term) Social Justice Warrior.<br /> WtA has never been a game about &quot;killing things&quot;, It is a game about saving the planet from its excess.<br /> One of the underlying themes of werewolf revised was that if fera had spent more time &quot;annoying their senators&quot; than slashing casually at things the overall situation would be better.<br /> <br /> Besides the tribes have always been about various kind of &quot;SWJ&quot; (again sorry for the term, I really think it's terrible)<br /> <br /> Wendigo with their problems with White colonialism, or the Children of Gaia, or the Furies who fought sexism and patriarchy, or the hyper-primitivist Red Talons, or against the bone gnawers Who lived in the lowest strata of society...in any case I think everything it's already there.<br /> <br /> Even the &quot;werewolves thrives on conflict&quot; it's wrong.<br /> <br /> The book are incredibly clear that conflict is killing the fera. Since the war of rage.<br /> The eternal conflict is not making the garou stronger, it's weakening them generation after generation.<br /> <br /> Even more, by embracing conflict blindly werewolves embrace the wyrm. There are reason if wisdom should go side by side with honor and valor.<br /> <br /> If you kill a pentex employee, maybe you will weaken pentex, but you will empower the urge wyrms in Malfeas.<br /> <br /> It is an underlying theme in the world or Darkness: the splats are blinded and distracted by trivial things that keep them from the important things. The blinding thing can varies, It can be Ascension War for mages, the jhyad for Vampires, or the internal conflicts of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> The Tribes are not stronger because Konietzko and Albrecht are at each other's throtat. Eternal strife just helps the wyrm.<br /> <br /> Just think about the story of the White Howlers. It's a giant metaphor of what is wrong with werewolves. You can't just throw yourself at the wyrm, Klaive in hands,fangs first. If you attack without wisdome, if you live just by rage, you are walking the spyral of the wyrm. The Howlers went on and one down the spyral, fighting at every level with even more rage. End in the end they were the Howlers no more, but the Black Spyral Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more. Well said.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T08:53:38-07:00","id":1249977,"title":"","content":"I could see them doubling down on the core themes of WtA as they move forward.<br /> <br /> Falling to rage is probably going to be their version of hunger dice where things that would piss of a Garou would raise your track rather than staying alive and using disciplines raises hunger. You can use your rage to fuel your power though by keeping control and you would make a control check instead of a rouse check maybe but this may just me looking at V5 and trying to port it over they may do something completely different like uses rage as the humanity tracker instead. Who knows? To lower your rage you have to do something that makes you feel better about the world like protect the woman that is being abused, meditate, or hunt to release some anger this would be their version of feeding and such.<br /> <br /> I am not sure their is a direct corrilation for blood resonance but I could see them having some sort of benifits for having more honor glory or wisdom and having deeds of renown be the way that these are increased which give you a fleeting bonus for the deed that you did maybe. Especially since degradation is not really a core concept of WtA, but loosing your self to your rage is.<br /> <br /> Gnosis is your connection to your spiritual side so they could do some sort of humanity treatment with this and makes stains be things that you do that are harmful to Gaia and this could also have chronicle tenants associated with it. They may also use this as the blood mechanic instead and have it be the thing that is like the hunger track.<br /> <br /> I could also see them doing away with the need to fuel gifts and abilities altogether for werewolves as well. I don't think I would have a problem with that. they would still need renown and rank requirements to use and learn them though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T09:03:17-07:00","id":1249978,"title":"","content":"I love me a good rant on how Core themes that are the very foundation of a game are &quot;ruining it&quot; complaining about SJW in Whitewolf games is like complaining about having to go into Dungeons and Fight Monsters in D&amp;D and not you know be able to use it as an elaborate farm simulator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T11:17:33-07:00","id":1250002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249944#post1249944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a curiosity, it was actually Philippos, Alexander's father.<br /> At Chaeronea they refused to surrender even after all their allies fled the battle and even if Philippos had tried to negotiate, suggesting to let them go away with all their armors, weapons and fallen comrades. To no avail, apparently, as the Band was firm in not retreating from a battlefield where their friends and lovers had shed their blood.<br /> And when the last member of the Sacred Band was put down, apparently Philippos seeing they were all fallen fighting, no one ran away, declared &quot;Perish any man who suspects that these men either did or suffered anything unseemly.&quot;<br /> or, as some more cynical viewers think, he just threatened of death penalty any of his soldiers or allies that would have dared to desecrate their corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>He built statues over where they fell to honour them, didn't he? There's something very noble about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T11:22:45-07:00","id":1250004,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11720\" data-vbnamecard=\"11720\">Redwulfe</a> in my experience Rage and Gnosis are treated as background stats; deeply important mechanically, but they're not RPed out. If you have a strong link to your spiritual side that should permeate your being. So yes, being able to lose Rage and Gnosis would be a good thing in my opinion. And being able to gain it without EXP in unusual circumstances could also be a very good thing. Treat it a little bit more like Humanity.<br /> <br /> High Gnosis; you should be RPing them as a tad more sage, although how this comes across can vary a lot. &quot;Sage&quot; doesn't have to mean peaceful or kind, but you should be more &quot;religious&quot; in terms of the Gaian creed as your Gnosis increases.<br /> <br /> High Rage; you should act more bestial and with an ineffable power. You should remind the ST that humans will be scared of you if they forget, and that you radiate a predatory menace.<br /> <br /> RPing someone with high rage and high gnosis would be a difficult balancing act of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T11:27:24-07:00","id":1250007,"title":"","content":"I don't think 2nd Inquisition works with Werewolf I like my SAD Doing powerless investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T12:05:47-07:00","id":1250021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250002#post1250002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He built statues over where they fell to honour them, didn't he? There's something very noble about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that too.<br /> What i was pointing out, though, was that their bravery was enough that he threatened of death, the men that had fought for him. That's a badass respect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T14:36:37-07:00","id":1250069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249937#post1249937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean we've slipped from &quot;I don't want it to be LGBT trendy SJW stuff&quot; to &quot;I don't want to have to consider the wellbeing of my players&quot;, this is starting to feel like quite the downward spiral (if you'll pardon the allusion).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people are misunderstanding what being told not to use content entails. I think, if most of the people here saying they don't want to leave content out, were asked by their gaming group to do so, they would.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm just picturing someone throwing a fit over not getting to use child murder fomor out of the blue XD<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Rage/Gnosis, I think Rage is EXTREMELY well discussed in the books. Most players just cannot deal with the Curse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T14:41:00-07:00","id":1250072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250069#post1250069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people are misunderstanding what being told not to use content entails. I think, if most of the people here saying they don't want to leave content out, were asked by their gaming group to do so, they would.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm just picturing someone throwing a fit over not getting to use child murder fomor out of the blue XD<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Rage/Gnosis, I think Rage is EXTREMELY well discussed in the books. Most players just cannot deal with the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I think the books cover it well, but the rules could be tweaked so that mechanically speaking it's harder to ignore the curse, you know? Although if people don't want to feel &quot;cursed&quot; when they play Garou, I guess they don't have to. If I were STing WTA I would play up the monstrous side of things a lot... have someone give a perspective of Garou and Fera as &quot;Gaian Hereditary Fomori&quot;, so-to-speak, and frame their rage as a true burden. But people don't have to RP out the curse side of things if they don't enjoy it I suppose...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-30-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T15:12:32-07:00","id":1250080,"title":"","content":"I think this is why I looked at Rage as the hunger mechanic for W5. Rage was a curse that had to be kept in check like hunger for vampires. The tag &quot;When will you rage?&quot; is much like the beast I am least the beast I become in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T15:30:37-07:00","id":1250086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250072#post1250072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah I think the books cover it well, but the rules could be tweaked so that mechanically speaking it's harder to ignore the curse, you know? Although if people don't want to feel &quot;cursed&quot; when they play Garou, I guess they don't have to. If I were STing WTA I would play up the monstrous side of things a lot... have someone give a perspective of Garou and Fera as &quot;Gaian Hereditary Fomori&quot;, so-to-speak, and frame their rage as a true burden. But people don't have to RP out the curse side of things if they don't enjoy it I suppose...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it already freaks out people passively. Rage 3 is 30% of the population avoiding you or something like that, so not a small number. Plus most garou change when they are early teens, so they typically lack any higher education. Not that trying to go to school when you freak people out, have insane trouble keeping your temper and CONSTANTLY smelling/seeing/feeling the wrongs around you, is easy.<br /> <br /> But that is not what players want, they don't want their ahroun to be a moocher being supported by their kinfolk. They don't want their character to be without a cool job or an army training. THat is the crux of the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T16:27:25-07:00","id":1250093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250086#post1250086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it already freaks out people passively. Rage 3 is 30% of the population avoiding you or something like that, so not a small number. Plus most garou change when they are early teens, so they typically lack any higher education. Not that trying to go to school when you freak people out, have insane trouble keeping your temper and CONSTANTLY smelling/seeing/feeling the wrongs around you, is easy.<br /> <br /> But that is not what players want, they don't want their ahroun to be a moocher being supported by their kinfolk. They don't want their character to be without a cool job or an army training. THat is the crux of the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I suppose the books could labour on the issue more; make it crystal clear that your Garou didn't train with SWAT force black ops alpha zero, and doesn't have a medical degree or anything like that. After all you can't rise through the ranks of most organizations if you freak out (in a big or small way) almost one third of people.<br /> <br /> It never occurred to me that Fera who lack Rage, like the Ananasi, are at a huge advantage. I mean is the Ananasi state a &quot;curse&quot;? The only horrible aspect I can see is how they tend to become more cold and detached as they age, but one could argue that's due to strengthening spiritual ties and advancing Gnosis, not anything biological or innate. Of course they rely on blood but they are well equipped to seek it, and don't fear gold or silver, or risk frenzy, and won't alienate anyone who they behave well around...<br /> <br /> And yes there's something less... romantic about your character being mother nature's DPS warrior, being cut off from society and relying on the care of your semi-supernatural cousins to survive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T18:04:45-07:00","id":1250108,"title":"","content":"My only great concern is the Rage Dice. Paradox can be described as a Scourge of the Gods over the mage's head. Hunger is the grip of the beast at the damned soul. Rage is not only a curse. Is also a gift. Rage is used to perform astonishing feats in blinding speed, strengthening the Garou in their holy war. Hunger is a Mechanic to represent the consequence of the vampiric powers, not the power that fuels it (as blood points was). Paradox is literally a increasing backlash of reality, not the source of magical powers. Their nature is be a problem in escalation, and so the mechanic of dices can work it well. But Garou are warriors, and rage is a gift of Luna. How use the mechanic of escalating problems to represent a spiritual gift of your super-human condition? Rage is fuel. Rage can protect you, high rage brings more chances to win in a fight. Rage brings the problems, but are not the core problem to the Garou's life like the Hunger for a vampire or Paradox to the mage. Rage, different paradox or hunger <i><b>never was a thing to avoid</b></i> in previous games. Different of Hunger and Paradox, Rage was ever a fix score evolving. In combat, you try don't be without rage points.<br /> <br /> Brings the curse of rage, the social detachment, the isolation and social awkwardness of a garou needs to be made with substitution of dices and random effects of mental outbreak driven your roleplaying?<br /> <br /> Another curiosity is: how will be the effects of Rage in the new system of combat? Spent Rage to attack multiple oponents? Werewolf is a game of a little more tactical combat. The new near-narrativist combat system is light rules and fluid. Eventually the combats are short and simple. Werewolf to some group has some elements of strategy and powebuilding. How to keep it in the new combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24565-gagarin-mal\u00e9","name":"Gagarin Mal\u00e9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T18:09:53-07:00","id":1250110,"title":"","content":"Building rage could be a double edged sword in the new system as well. Say you do have a rage track and things that tick you off rases that. But at the same time your powers become more active as you rais it as well.<br /> <br /> For example to powers don't become active until your rage hits certain levels and you have rage dice that could cause messy criticals. You need to fuel your powers but at the risk of loosing complete control might be interesting to balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T19:49:15-07:00","id":1250147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250080#post1250080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is why I looked at Rage as the hunger mechanic for W5. Rage was a curse that had to be kept in check like hunger for vampires. The tag &quot;When will you rage?&quot; is much like the beast I am least the beast I become in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When will you Rage?&quot;, and later in W20, &quot;How will you Rage?&quot; were calls to action, not a bereavement of being between a rock and a hard place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T19:51:35-07:00","id":1250148,"title":"","content":"I kinda like the rock and a hard place feel. I think that is why I liked forsaken a bit better. That I I never really liked sept politics. With vampire it was the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T00:20:30-07:00","id":1250191,"title":"","content":"Which is... just asking for all the fanbase upset we're seeing with V5 in W5. De-emphasizing Septs and making things more pack focused is just going to be &quot;Forsakenization&quot; and so on.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about &quot;what do you want in a werewolf game.&quot; We're talking about what a 5th edition of an existing franchise might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T02:20:18-07:00","id":1250207,"title":"","content":"Well, I think if it goes V5-ways, than septs will be strengthened and tribes will be watered down. Global plots and communication - possibly umbra travel - will be reduced and local conflicts will be more in the focus. It is a &quot;Forsakenization&quot; - possibly, or a 'Requiumination' maybe.<br /> <br /> Personally, I find a lot of the changes BNS brought into Werewolf wrong, and also changes W20 brought. I talked to some of the authors back in NOLA, and got where they were coming from, but didn't think their solutions to problems were that well thought out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T13:01:55-07:00","id":1250308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249924#post1249924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that LGBT people make up a significant percentage of the population, including them in tabletop games isn't a political move. It's apolitical.<br /> <br /> Excluding LGBT people, however, can be a political move on the part of developers.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;LGBT inclusion is just trendy&amp;quot; unknowlingly means, in many cases, &amp;quot;this is new and confusing to me and is probably being included to make me uncomfortable.&amp;quot; It's not that any of this is new (I can show you cultures that have existed for thousands of years with a &amp;quot;third gender&amp;quot;, and examples of publicly accepted homosexual romance/lust in ancient civilizations like Rome and Athens and Sparta), it's that it *feels* new because more people can be more honest about who they are and don't feel the need to hide it. No one is going to apologize if it upsets you.<br /> <br /> All it takes is a sidebar explaining that the Furies accept non-binary and trans women into their ranks (perhaps with some of their Elders being very conservative on the issue and only wanting &amp;quot;women born women&amp;quot; among them). That won't turn Werewolf into a Lesbian Feelings Simulator; these Furies would still be tearing banes and fomori apart, the table would just feel more inclusive to certain people who want to play. It can be an action-fueled murder-fest and also be inclusive and positive. And do the Litany's demands that Garou don't lay with other Garou apply to same-sex couples? These are issues which would be very important to a lot of people in the Garou Nation. Greek armies sometimes paired young men together and encouraged them to fall in love (either platonically or romantically) so that they would fight well to protect eachother, watch eachother's backs. I bring this up because it shows that you can tell a story about homoeroticism which is still incredibly violent and action-driven.<br /> <br /> Speaking of LGBT stuff, can someone remind me if anyone other than the Ananasi can learn that Gift where they become the opposite sex? Obviously most use it for disguise or seduction (and in extreme cases for fertility), but there's definitely room for someone to play a Loki style character who flips between man and woman depending on the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really disagree with you, LGBTQ inclusion has grown trendy and is in many cases all about image. I\u2019m a bisexual man and a very passionate, longtime queer activist (20 years plus of marching and fighting now) and I see A LOT of queer inclusion being done sheerly for image reasons.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying that\u2019s what the other poster was talking about, I just think that there\u2019s so much bullshit fake acceptance now that\u2019s really only done out of a bullshit desire to look good. I don\u2019t think white Wolf is emblematic of that, they\u2019ve always been pretty good right from the start, back when it was really hard to be queer accepting and still sell a game but man... there are so many bullshit marketing moves designed to capitalize on queer acceptance nowadays.<br /> <br /> Of course you may not agree but I see this as a real issue, I feel turning queer acceptance into a fad is not a way to create true acceptance, it does not have the depth or the sincerity that people really wrestling with their reluctance or intolerance and coming to abandon it actually has.<br /> <br /> And I wonder, if that superficial acceptance that was brought into prevalence by a change in trend falls out of fashion, what are we going to be left with?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just some food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T13:40:59-07:00","id":1250315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250308#post1250308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually really disagree with you, LGBTQ inclusion has grown trendy and is in many cases all about image. I\u2019m a bisexual man and a very passionate, longtime queer activist (20 years plus of marching and fighting now) and I see A LOT of queer inclusion being done sheerly for image reasons.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying that\u2019s what the other poster was talking about, I just think that there\u2019s so much bullshit fake acceptance now that\u2019s really only done out of a bullshit desire to look good. I don\u2019t think white Wolf is emblematic of that, they\u2019ve always been pretty good right from the start, back when it was really hard to be queer accepting and still sell a game but man... there are so many bullshit marketing moves designed to capitalize on queer acceptance nowadays.<br /> <br /> Of course you may not agree but I see this as a real issue, I feel turning queer acceptance into a fad is not a way to create true acceptance, it does not have the depth or the sincerity that people really wrestling with their reluctance or intolerance and coming to abandon it actually has.<br /> <br /> And I wonder, if that superficial acceptance that was brought into prevalence by a change in trend falls out of fashion, what are we going to be left with?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just some food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Rainbow Capitalism is an issue; weapons manufacturers and crooked financial institutions and politicians in bed with both showing up draped in a gay pride flag for one day, talking about how #progressive they are, but it's quite transparent. Most of the time I've heard people talking about LGBT stuff being trendy it's when I hear people asking bisexual or trans people whether it's a &quot;fad&quot; or something like that (and I've been asked that question myself; apparently people will date people they're not attracted to or take hormones to be trendy these days, which is quite astounding! ;-) ) and while there are a few voices talking about &quot;trendy teens&quot; who aren't *really* queer, most of the community knows what is what. For every person talking about transtrenders (see what they did there?!) who are just doing it to be cool, there are 100 people who don't gatekeep the community and are accepting.<br /> <br /> So there's definitely a market in talking about LGBT pride to score points and look progressive (look at Pride sponsorship; you'd almost forget that Pride was originally a riot), and there's definitely a market in people saying &quot;oh wow they're just doing this to look trendy or progressive&quot; (look at any of the Youtube careers built almost entirely off of this idea), but both of these are marginal in my opinion. They don't reflect reality, they're just noisy and attention-grabbing ideas.<br /> <br /> And at the end of the day we agree; I don't think that white wolf or onyx path or any of the writers of WoD books have ever included LGBT stuff &quot;just to be trendy&quot;. They did it before it was widely accepted and just treated it like it was a normal thing. And that's the most important thing in this discussion really. And while it's hard to determine a person's true feelings on these topics just from their writing, I do feel like it's quite telling if a person believes that W20 or V20 or M20 were &quot;trendy virtue signaling&quot; or whatever. All I can see is someone saying &quot;I think these things were included purely to pander to people who aren't like me, I think it must have been done without sincerity (because I don't believe that anyone would ever do it sincerely, and I think that it subtracts from the book's value&quot;. There's something... insidious about it. I get this nagging feeling that there's no right way to include these things for some people, that there's no acceptable amount of representation. So I take &quot;oh yeah I agree with it in principle but it's gone too far&quot;, another common argument, with a huge pinch of salt. You see it with any argument. It's funny how everyone is okay with civil partnership, it's just gay marriage they disagree with. And before that, of course we're all okay with it being legal to be homosexual, we just disagree with any kind of civil partnership. And so on and so forth. People will happily concede every argument which has already been lost after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-31-2018, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T15:57:46-07:00","id":1250341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250315#post1250315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Rainbow Capitalism is an issue; weapons manufacturers and crooked financial institutions and politicians in bed with both showing up draped in a gay pride flag for one day, talking about how #progressive they are, but it's quite transparent. Most of the time I've heard people talking about LGBT stuff being trendy it's when I hear people asking bisexual or trans people whether it's a &amp;quot;fad&amp;quot; or something like that (and I've been asked that question myself; apparently people will date people they're not attracted to or take hormones to be trendy these days, which is quite astounding! ;-) ) and while there are a few voices talking about &amp;quot;trendy teens&amp;quot; who aren't *really* queer, most of the community knows what is what. For every person talking about transtrenders (see what they did there?!) who are just doing it to be cool, there are 100 people who don't gatekeep the community and are accepting.<br /> <br /> So there's definitely a market in talking about LGBT pride to score points and look progressive (look at Pride sponsorship; you'd almost forget that Pride was originally a riot), and there's definitely a market in people saying &amp;quot;oh wow they're just doing this to look trendy or progressive&amp;quot; (look at any of the Youtube careers built almost entirely off of this idea), but both of these are marginal in my opinion. They don't reflect reality, they're just noisy and attention-grabbing ideas.<br /> <br /> And at the end of the day we agree; I don't think that white wolf or onyx path or any of the writers of WoD books have ever included LGBT stuff &amp;quot;just to be trendy&amp;quot;. They did it before it was widely accepted and just treated it like it was a normal thing. And that's the most important thing in this discussion really. And while it's hard to determine a person's true feelings on these topics just from their writing, I do feel like it's quite telling if a person believes that W20 or V20 or M20 were &amp;quot;trendy virtue signaling&amp;quot; or whatever. All I can see is someone saying &amp;quot;I think these things were included purely to pander to people who aren't like me, I think it must have been done without sincerity (because I don't believe that anyone would ever do it sincerely, and I think that it subtracts from the book's value&amp;quot;. There's something... insidious about it. I get this nagging feeling that there's no right way to include these things for some people, that there's no acceptable amount of representation. So I take &amp;quot;oh yeah I agree with it in principle but it's gone too far&amp;quot;, another common argument, with a huge pinch of salt. You see it with any argument. It's funny how everyone is okay with civil partnership, it's just gay marriage they disagree with. And before that, of course we're all okay with it being legal to be homosexual, we just disagree with any kind of civil partnership. And so on and so forth. People will happily concede every argument which has already been lost after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually feel that same sex marriage really was breaking new ground, because it was in fact essentially kicking the door in on the religious institutions and basically saying that they have no right decline to marry us anymore than they have the right to deny marrying any straight couple. <br /> <br /> In that regard, the quality of the social change is different, as we are now entering into the sphere of ancient religious institutionalized thought inside the actual institutions themselves. The legalization of homosexuality was more of a societal concern on a secular level (though of course the religious radicals wanted to ensure that it did not happen).<br /> <br /> Like civil partnership, the legalization of homosexuality was more of a secular change, though the former did skirt the religious realm more than the latter. Fortunately for us, the religious radicals were right when they predicted that same sex civil unions would bring about the end of traditional opposite sex marriage! Who would\u2019ve known we would be so pleased to see their worst predictions for our society come true! <br /> <br /> Still though, I do worry that children today are being taught to simply accept the queer community and that this message is being forced too aggressively on them. The reason for that is because, in our messages to \u201cjust accept\u201d, we often do not ask them how they feel and why they do not accept the queer people in those cases where they feel that way. As such, I feel we are neglecting to make arguments in favour of acceptance that actually address these people\u2019s real feelings and thus, we are merely pushing an attitude onto them without the essential element of an intellectual discussion where we give them the chance to air their thoughts and then address them. <br /> <br /> I feel that without addressing the root causes of their concerns/biases we are doing them a disservice no matter how prejudiced their opinions are (note that I am talking about young people exclusively) and that the push for acceptance only really breeds a superficial acceptance in those minds that do not do the work of questioning and divorcing themselves from antiqueer values on their own time. <br /> <br /> Sadly, the message some members of our society spread \u201cif you don\u2019t accept queer people you\u2019re an asshole and end of discussion\u201d only breeds pushback, resentment and often worse sentiments.<br /> <br /> I am aware that this point has strayed far afield from your original point and even further from the topic of W5 but I felt compelled to express my concerns. It is because I am so often troubled these days by what I see as a growing and increasingly hostile method of trying to increase the level of queer acceptance through means that will only engender push back in the long run, that I feel the need to speak about this issue where I get the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T16:11:23-07:00","id":1250343,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Zennis;n1250341]<br /> <br /> I actually feel that same sex marriage really was breaking new ground, because it was in fact essentially kicking the door in on the religious institutions and basically saying that they have no right decline to marry us anymore than they have the right to deny marrying any straight couple./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It was breaking ground but not in the way you are thinking. A Church can and will decline people for marriage. A church still has this right. What makes civil unions complete crap second class options is entirely a secular issue. Civil Unions don't have 200+ years of definition under the law. Marriage does. Marriage has all sorts of secondary effects that are baked in on all levels of government that you can't just make something that &quot;is just as good&quot; without you know changing all those thousands of laws.<br /> <br /> Churches still have the right to be bigoted I can name one recently that turned down someone's marriage because it was cross racial. They can do that. But a Judge can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T17:01:16-07:00","id":1250353,"title":"","content":"Ok. Super basic. If we look at V5 metaplot what will become of W5? Garou Nation destroyed as a cohesive whole, some tribes will switch allegiance from Gaia or perhaps the nation will break up into smaller sects. A number of important Caerns will be destroyed in wildly unlikely but successful raids by humans, increased balkanisation and some sort of 'Avatar Storm' to limit Moon Bridges. A lot of Elder Garou will die and or be incapacitated and Ronin or Skin Dancers will become a major part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Ok, thats a pretty straight swap and a bunch of that won't happen ( I hope) but there will almost certainly be a fair amount of Forsaken mechanics swapped in, in a somewhat altered manner, as Requiem was into V5. We can hope that the truly weird shit that BNS has done to the WtA LARP wont make an appearance but given the shit WW have pulled with WtA20th products who knows?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T19:34:50-07:00","id":1250375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250315#post1250315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And at the end of the day we agree; I don't think that white wolf or onyx path or any of the writers of WoD books have ever included LGBT stuff &quot;just to be trendy&quot;. They did it before it was widely accepted and just treated it like it was a normal thing. And that's the most important thing in this discussion really. And while it's hard to determine a person's true feelings on these topics just from their writing, I do feel like it's quite telling if a person believes that W20 or V20 or M20 were &quot;trendy virtue signaling&quot; or whatever. All I can see is someone saying &quot;I think these things were included purely to pander to people who aren't like me, I think it must have been done without sincerity (because I don't believe that anyone would ever do it sincerely, and I think that it subtracts from the book's value&quot;. There's something... insidious about it. I get this nagging feeling that there's no right way to include these things for some people, that there's no acceptable amount of representation. So I take &quot;oh yeah I agree with it in principle but it's gone too far&quot;, another common argument, with a huge pinch of salt. You see it with any argument. It's funny how everyone is okay with civil partnership, it's just gay marriage they disagree with. And before that, of course we're all okay with it being legal to be homosexual, we just disagree with any kind of civil partnership. And so on and so forth. People will happily concede every argument which has already been lost after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't help but to add a reaction to this. You know, I liked that the old WW games included &quot;progressive elements&quot;, because yes, they treated it, like normal things. They just were. Today, I frequently feel pointed pandering and virtue signaling indeed, from every strata of entertainment industry and that is, sorry, but bad and that is what turns people off.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I know full well I won't be popular on these forums (just see how the discussion istantly started to be about LGBTQ people and the depiction of tribes) by saying that, but here it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, yes, Werewolf was essentially about things that, in the US, were and are considered as leftist and progressive talking points. And I liked it for that. I have a degree in nature conservation engineering in no small part because of Werewolf's influence on me as a teen. However, I, as a Hungarian, don't care about the excesses of US politics and them seeping into everything. I don't want shoehorning tribes or anything else, to fit current political narratives and picking sides, as they did with the V5 Brujah. I want them to present conflicts and ideas, yes, but not like that.<br /> <br /> I want the game about horribly flawed shapechangers trying to save the planet, while struggling with their own issues (including LGBTQ people in cases of some specific tribes, though not necessarily all of them going super-accepting entirely, because that would be unfaithful to them). I want the clashes of cultures, of old and new, of spiritual and practical.<br /> <br /> I don't want the game about POC LGBTQ werewolves fighting the evil white cishetero capitalist male supremacy and going vegan.<br /> <br /> Yes I exaggerated, but I hope I managed to get to the point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T19:52:42-07:00","id":1250382,"title":"","content":"Moving beyond the exaggeration though, you can't have one without the other, because one of the biggest &quot;battlegrounds&quot; of clashing cultures and struggling over issues in modern society is the function of institutional and intersectional inequality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T20:42:31-07:00","id":1250390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250375#post1250375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can't help but to add a reaction to this. You know, I liked that the old WW games included &quot;progressive elements&quot;, because yes, they treated it, like normal things. They just were. Today, I frequently feel pointed pandering and virtue signaling indeed, from every strata of entertainment industry and that is, sorry, but bad and that is what turns people off.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I know full well I won't be popular on these forums (just see how the discussion istantly started to be about LGBTQ people and the depiction of tribes) by saying that, but here it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, yes, Werewolf was essentially about things that, in the US, were and are considered as leftist and progressive talking points. And I liked it for that. I have a degree in nature conservation engineering in no small part because of Werewolf's influence on me as a teen. However, I, as a Hungarian, don't care about the excesses of US politics and them seeping into everything. I don't want shoehorning tribes or anything else, to fit current political narratives and picking sides, as they did with the V5 Brujah. I want them to present conflicts and ideas, yes, but not like that.<br /> <br /> I want the game about horribly flawed shapechangers trying to save the planet, while struggling with their own issues (including LGBTQ people in cases of some specific tribes, though not necessarily all of them going super-accepting entirely, because that would be unfaithful to them). I want the clashes of cultures, of old and new, of spiritual and practical.<br /> <br /> I don't want the game about POC LGBTQ werewolves fighting the evil white cishetero capitalist male supremacy and going vegan.<br /> <br /> Yes I exaggerated, but I hope I managed to get to the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point reads as &quot;I don't remember a large number of factions from the game and what's important to them, what they did, or what they do&quot; because W:tA has largely been about all of those points at the end except going vegan (at least, for Garou and Fera; Kami are different).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T20:57:22-07:00","id":1250393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250375#post1250375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but to add a reaction to this. You know, I liked that the old WW games included &quot;progressive elements&quot;, because yes, they treated it, like normal things. They just were. Today, I frequently feel pointed pandering and virtue signaling indeed, from every strata of entertainment industry and that is, sorry, but bad and that is what turns people off.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I know full well I won't be popular on these forums (just see how the discussion istantly started to be about LGBTQ people and the depiction of tribes) by saying that, but here it is.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, Werewolf was essentially about things that, in the US, were and are considered as leftist and progressive talking points. And I liked it for that. I have a degree in nature conservation engineering in no small part because of Werewolf's influence on me as a teen. However, I, as a Hungarian, don't care about the excesses of US politics and them seeping into everything. I don't want shoehorning tribes or anything else, to fit current political narratives and picking sides, as they did with the V5 Brujah. I want them to present conflicts and ideas, yes, but not like that.<br /> <br /> I want the game about horribly flawed shapechangers trying to save the planet, while struggling with their own issues (including LGBTQ people in cases of some specific tribes, though not necessarily all of them going super-accepting entirely, because that would be unfaithful to them). I want the clashes of cultures, of old and new, of spiritual and practical.<br /> <br /> I don't want the game about POC LGBTQ werewolves fighting the evil white cishetero capitalist male supremacy and going vegan.<br /> <br /> Yes I exaggerated, but I hope I managed to get to the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the game has any sign of showing that it will ever be &quot;poc lgbtq werewolves fighting blah blah blah&quot;; It's just never been moving toward it. You fear really has no backing, so I guess.. don't worry? When has the makers of the game shown they want this at all? Honestly, it sounds more like a fake argument, as if to make it sound like poc or lgbtq individuals would want that... which again, they don't. ( to be clear, I don't mean that you posted this as a fake argument to fuel something, just that &quot;Zomg, the SJW POC LBTQ are out to get your personal christmas!&quot; is thrown around as if.. real?) They go through a lot of crap, and I think I can safely say they'd rather have the game show it's a struggle against a lot of stupid people, and that Garou are still at heart.. a group of stupid people.. wolves.. spirits.. you get what I mean.<br /> <br /> It's always been about flawed tribes, fighting to try to make things work to fight back a bigger threat before it made the world explode. Honestly I think their book changing ways seemed like, to some, &quot;pandering&quot; (Honestly both sides think they pandered to the opposite on this one). I Disagree, as I honestly have had huge discussion about Black Furies, Spirits, trans individuals, and trans garou before it came out and this book finally helped me finish the discussion. I don't think it's pandering at all, just helping shift the norm questions to today's norms, as I now have trans players.. and they have good questions that the old books didn't answer, and I can only do my best as storyteller. None of that, though, shows they think that's what the tribes are about (I mean most of those notes were side notes)... and I don't see any people here on the forums, or in my games, that would want the game to be about that.. so &quot;That&quot;, I am less worried about. I am FAR more worried they will make the tribes more bland... less human... less relatable. That I do worry, as it's far easier to make every tribe awesome perfect, then it is to make them realistic and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13744-ishtar","user":"Ishtar","date":". 09-01-2018, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13744-ishtar","name":"Ishtar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T06:40:18-07:00","id":1250441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ishtar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250393#post1250393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always been about flawed tribes, fighting to try to make things work to fight back a bigger threat before it made the world explode. Honestly I think their book changing ways seemed like, to some, &quot;pandering&quot; (Honestly both sides think they pandered to the opposite on this one). I Disagree, as I honestly have had huge discussion about Black Furies, Spirits, trans individuals, and trans garou before it came out and this book finally helped me finish the discussion. I don't think it's pandering at all, just helping shift the norm questions to today's norms, as I now have trans players.. and they have good questions that the old books didn't answer, and I can only do my best as storyteller. None of that, though, shows they think that's what the tribes are about (I mean most of those notes were side notes)... and I don't see any people here on the forums, or in my games, that would want the game to be about that.. so &quot;That&quot;, I am less worried about. I am FAR more worried they will make the tribes more bland... less human... less relatable. That I do worry, as it's far easier to make every tribe awesome perfect, then it is to make them realistic and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Ways is not the best to me, because it included unneeded themes (such as Furies and Red Talons kidnapping male homids to have sex with their wolf kin) and when it tried to discuss homosexuality in the metis chapter, it felt really demeaning. In a &quot;Look, they are OK with the gayz&quot; way, rather than discussing how the tribe would see it broadly. It felt like it was constantly yelling at homophobic readers how -wrong- they were. It didn't feel grounded in the setting.<br /> <br /> What I fear the most, is that the BNS MET book serves as the groundwork for the new edition. It is very hard for me to get over them taking a tribe most see as unplayable, and then making it worse. Rather than actually trying to give Red Talons a make-over to make them actually playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T07:54:59-07:00","id":1250450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1249928#post1249928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, in ancient greece the Theban Sacred Band (300 warriors, 150 couples) was the most elite unit in Greece. So incredible it was that the Sacred Band destroyed the Spartiates at Leuttra, and at the time Spartiates were known to had no rival in open field battles.<br /> After Leuttra the Band was undefeated for 30 years, and perished only when it met Alexander in the field.<br /> <br /> So getting homosexuals in the tribes really doens't diminish the &quot;action-drive&quot; of the setting, it just allows more people to play freely the game.<br /> Besides, I do not really recall &quot;homophobia&quot; as one of the core theme of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I agree with your point, the battle of Leuktra was won due to the genius plan of Epameinondas, the Theban general. Without going into much detail, Greeks had the tradition of having their stronger warriors on the right wing of the phalanx, to counteract the right-hand drift. So knowing that the Spartans would be there, he basically confronted the strong Spartan right wing of about 12 men deep phalanx with a 50!! men deep formation and cavalry, the Sacred Band was indeed part of this formation. Then to nullify the weakness that created in the middle and right parts of his formation he had his army advance in a diagonal fashion, creating the now famous Echelon formation. Obviously, the Spartans were not expecting such an onslaught from what should be the weak part of the enemy army and lost the engagement suffering heaving losses including most of the Ippeis, the famous 300-men contingent that was charged with protecting their kings.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Mentioned right after, am I blind? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> [[[It might be interesting to mention that the Sacred Band met its end at the hands of a 16-year old Alexander leading his father's companion cavalry, at the battle of Chaeronea where theychoose to fight to the death even when the battle was lost and the remains of the Theban army had surrendered.]]]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 09-01-2018, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T09:37:48-07:00","id":1250469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250382#post1250382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving beyond the exaggeration though, you can't have one without the other, because one of the biggest &quot;battlegrounds&quot; of clashing cultures and struggling over issues in modern society is the function of institutional and intersectional inequality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing is and I won't be popular for saying this either, it's not, really. Most average people aren't activists on the left side and they have very little encounters with these things. But I'm living in Hungary, not on the West Coast of the US, so that could be a factor. But even then, some of my friends are living in Britain and they say they don't encounter these things too much either. I think the people who deals with these things a lot and have a personal interest/stake int he culture war are a bubble. A pretty substantial bubble, mind you, especially in the US, but still a bubble.<br /> <br /> But for me, it's mostly about how much the game internalizes specific narratives and how biased it is toward political sides and ideologies. Allow me an example: the blurb about the role of trans people in magical traditions and ancient societies in M20 wasn't pandering in my eyes, I liked it. What I read about the Mage Prelude mobile game's shoehorning the Traditions and the Technocracy into the narrative surrounding the European migration crisis (Technocracy=fascist conservative nationalists opposing mass migration= bad / Traditions=good guys=refugees and refugee helpers) was a gross and bad oversimplification of the whole thing and an unfaithful portrayal of the factions (and the real-world problem) and it was definitely a reflection of WW members' political views and I'd say pandering to a side. Or that I didn't feel Anarchs Unbound to be pandering, it was critical, but pictured the Anarchs as competent. The V5 Brujah writeup, I feel is pandering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250390#post1250390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your point reads as &quot;I don't remember a large number of factions from the game and what's important to them, what they did, or what they do&quot; because W:tA has largely been about all of those points at the end except going vegan (at least, for Garou and Fera; Kami are different).</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>Or you know, we might have different reads on things in the game, because of different backgrounds and we might put emphasis in our minds on different things from what we read... I know it's hard to imagine, but trust me, it's possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ishtar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250393#post1250393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the game has any sign of showing that it will ever be &quot;poc lgbtq werewolves fighting blah blah blah&quot;; It's just never been moving toward it. You fear really has no backing, so I guess.. don't worry? When has the makers of the game shown they want this at all? Honestly, it sounds more like a fake argument, as if to make it sound like poc or lgbtq individuals would want that... which again, they don't. ( to be clear, I don't mean that you posted this as a fake argument to fuel something, just that &quot;Zomg, the SJW POC LBTQ are out to get your personal christmas!&quot; is thrown around as if.. real?) They go through a lot of crap, and I think I can safely say they'd rather have the game show it's a struggle against a lot of stupid people, and that Garou are still at heart.. a group of stupid people.. wolves.. spirits.. you get what I mean.<br /> <br /> It's always been about flawed tribes, fighting to try to make things work to fight back a bigger threat before it made the world explode. Honestly I think their book changing ways seemed like, to some, &quot;pandering&quot; (Honestly both sides think they pandered to the opposite on this one). I Disagree, as I honestly have had huge discussion about Black Furies, Spirits, trans individuals, and trans garou before it came out and this book finally helped me finish the discussion. I don't think it's pandering at all, just helping shift the norm questions to today's norms, as I now have trans players.. and they have good questions that the old books didn't answer, and I can only do my best as storyteller. None of that, though, shows they think that's what the tribes are about (I mean most of those notes were side notes)... and I don't see any people here on the forums, or in my games, that would want the game to be about that.. so &quot;That&quot;, I am less worried about. I am FAR more worried they will make the tribes more bland... less human... less relatable. That I do worry, as it's far easier to make every tribe awesome perfect, then it is to make them realistic and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>What could skew my perception, definitely is, honestly, this forum, because it has a certain visitor batch and these things are frequent and heated talking points. However, I'd acknowledge that the books weren't centered on these things, yes. I'm just wary about the next edition, since what WW did with the abovementioned things aren't reassuring me that the game won't be choke-full of blatant pandering (and changing of setting lore and tribes and such, to fit their preferred narrative), since it's a lot more political even than Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-04-2018, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T14:18:47-07:00","id":1250533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250469#post1250469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing is and I won't be popular for saying this either, it's not, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on... what exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most average people aren't activists on the left side and they have very little encounters with these things. </div> </div> </div>That's <b>why</b> it's such a big problem. Most people encounter this all the time and don't see it, and thus allow the problems to persist. You don't need to be an activist to interact with the problem, and the lack of open acknowledgement is what allows people to dig in and say &quot;Well I don't see it, so how bad can it really be?&quot;<br /> <br /> The vast majority of people aren't climate change activists, scientists, or even people that can directly link a negative change in their lives brought on by climate change. But the climate is still changing, and the impact of those changes impact pretty much everyone even if they don't see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm living in Hungary, not on the West Coast of the US, so that could be a factor. </div> </div> </div>So... tell me again how there's no intersectional or institutional social problems in Hungary regarding it's Romani minority population? Why are they still poorer, less educated, less likely to have significant assets, and more likely to live in segregation from the majority Hungarian ethnic peoples despite having equal rights and &quot;opportunities&quot; and the days of open legal discrimination are over?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I don't live on the West Coast either... I live in the Rust Belt. But hey, lets stereotype Americans by where they live because that's totally a good way to prove you're critically thinking about social issues and trying to see what's going on rather than relying on talking points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even then, some of my friends are living in Britain and they say they don't encounter these things too much either. </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't see it, so it can't be happening,&quot; is not a good argument. The UK has a lot of problems along these lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the people who deals with these things a lot and have a personal interest/stake int he culture war are a bubble. A pretty substantial bubble, mind you, especially in the US, but still a bubble. </div> </div> </div>You live in a country where 96% of the population is the same ethnic group... what's your basis exactly for proclaiming people that live in far more diverse countries are living in bubbles when it comes to these topics?<br /> <br /> And when you go to parts of the USA that are likewise overwhelming people of European decent... we here the same exact kind of stuff you're saying, &quot;we don't see it,&quot; &quot;it's a coastal elite thing,&quot; &quot;those people are just in the leftist bubble.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's just talking about local politics. We're not even getting into the global issues that we see in South America, Africa, and large portions of Asia, that stem from centuries of European colonialism, followed by Cold War proxy fighting, and then economic exploitation under global trade regimes. <br /> <br /> This has been an essential theme of WtA from the beginning. You can't stop murder by killing murderers. You can't stop wars by killing all the soldiers. The Garou are warriors trying to stop things you can't end with violence. Ending them requires understanding the complexity of why things are happening, historical context, and addressing that most of these problems require long term investment to counter regression.<br /> <br /> If all you do is blow up factories, you'll never stop Pentex. You have to understand the systems Pentex exploits to maintain it's profits despite whatever physical damage you inflict on it's subsidiaries. You have to figure out how to alter cultures to remove the demand for Pentex's products. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But for me, it's mostly about how much the game internalizes specific narratives and how biased it is toward political sides and ideologies. </div> </div> </div>But your examples aren't about this. M20 still has the Technocracy as bad fascists and the Traditions as good minority rights activists. M20 just has the space to be a lot more nuanced and detailed than the Prelude did (not that I disagree that the Prelude is bad for it, and the refugee crisis in particular wasn't a good choice in my mind if you want a more black &amp; white issue for the Ascension warriors to square off over instead of a much more messy and muddy one).<br /> <br /> Pandering is really a matter of presentation not the core content. And even then, plenty of pandering is so minor that it's not really a big deal. There's been lots of token minority characters in films that haven't been hurtful to those minorities, or actively made the films worse for anyone that's not racist. It might not be real representation that makes the world more egalitarian, but it doesn't drag media into some inescapable slippery slope either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or you know, we might have different reads on things in the game, because of different backgrounds and we might put emphasis in our minds on different things from what we read... I know it's hard to imagine, but trust me, it's possible. </div> </div> </div>There's a pretty big difference between variance in interpretations based on our different backgrounds, and a statement that seems to forget the core and explicitly stated themes of half the Tribes, and that one of the big enemies in the game is Pentex.<br /> <br /> There is no level of good faith reading of WtA that allows for our differences to include, &quot;WtA hasn't always included minority groups fighting corrupt capitalists&quot; as a fair statement about the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T18:11:04-07:00","id":1250581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250533#post1250533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on... what exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, language barriers here, because this thing is quite deep, but i try to do my best.<br /> <br /> In my eyes, and you'd likely disagree with that and it's okay, I know we have very different worldviews, inequalities between countries, social classes, ethnicities, cultures etc. is indeed one of the biggest clashes of ideas and policies and all that today, but when you say &quot;institutional and intersectional inequality&quot;, I see it as a certain narrative and talking points more confined to certain places and groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's <b>why</b> it's such a big problem. Most people encounter this all the time and don't see it, and thus allow the problems to persist. You don't need to be an activist to interact with the problem, and the lack of open acknowledgement is what allows people to dig in and say &quot;Well I don't see it, so how bad can it really be?&quot;<br /> <br /> The vast majority of people aren't climate change activists, scientists, or even people that can directly link a negative change in their lives brought on by climate change. But the climate is still changing, and the impact of those changes impact pretty much everyone even if they don't see it. </div> </div> </div>Except climate change is mostly acknowledged as fact in the scientific world and have an influence on everyone's life. In contrast, lots of the leftist social talking points are much more debated and much more confined. Like, trans rights, problems and issues. It's a very small percent of the population which is actually affected by it. I'm not saying it's unimportant and that we shouldn't try to solve them (though the &quot;how&quot; of solving them is, again, highly debated, as factions can't even agree with the actual problems), but most people aren't affected by them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So... tell me again how there's no intersectional or institutional social problems in Hungary regarding it's Romani minority population? Why are they still poorer, less educated, less likely to have significant assets, and more likely to live in segregation from the majority Hungarian ethnic peoples despite having equal rights and &quot;opportunities&quot; and the days of open legal discrimination are over? </div> </div> </div>Social problems? Sure and it's extremely complicated and it's a shame governments from either side couldn't improve the situation a lot for decades. But again, &quot;intersectional&quot; and &quot;institutional&quot; implies a certain narrative and approach which is not necessarily applicable.<br /> <br /> I think the main thing is, that the problems in different regions are not the same, as well as the surrounding cultures and as well as how people approach them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and I don't live on the West Coast either... I live in the Rust Belt. But hey, lets stereotype Americans by where they live because that's totally a good way to prove you're critically thinking about social issues and trying to see what's going on rather than relying on talking points. </div> </div> </div>Ok, you're an exception, congrats! Naturally, stereotypes are not absolute truths, but they usually have an ammount of truth, that's just how it works.<br /> <br /> And thank you, I usually try to see what's going on, instead of buying into narratives and beliefs. That's why people on either extreme side of politics tend to not like me, because I call bullshit on bigot and senseless righties just as weel as on bigot and senseless leftists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I don't see it, so it can't be happening,&quot; is not a good argument. The UK has a lot of problems along these lines. </div> </div> </div>Oh, it wasn't about ethnic minorities, they're certianly encountering <i>that</i>. It was more about the gender and feminism-related stuff and I have gay individuals and women among them.<br /> <br /> Even then, yes, &quot;I don't see it, so it can't be happening,&quot; is not an argument, but I didn1t mean that. I meant that certain things are just not widespread problems for most of the population.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You live in a country where 96% of the population is the same ethnic group... what's your basis exactly for proclaiming people that live in far more diverse countries are living in bubbles when it comes to these topics? </div> </div> </div>In a part yes, because they're experiencing <i>their </i>culture and problems and that experience isn't necessarily applicable to other regions. But it's not just that, it's also an ideological bubble and a cultural and sub-cultural bubble.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when you go to parts of the USA that are likewise overwhelming people of European decent... we here the same exact kind of stuff you're saying, &quot;we don't see it,&quot; &quot;it's a coastal elite thing,&quot; &quot;those people are just in the leftist bubble.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Aaaaand you guys kept dismissing them and kept calling them names and you've got Trump. Congratulations.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the leftist urban (mostly Budapest) intelligentsia here is doing the same for a long time and we've got the third 2/3 win of Orb\u00e1n this spring. I'm not happy at all, because I really don't like what they are doing and their mentality, but honestly? The left there made its own grave too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's just talking about local politics. We're not even getting into the global issues that we see in South America, Africa, and large portions of Asia, that stem from centuries of European colonialism, followed by Cold War proxy fighting, and then economic exploitation under global trade regimes. </div> </div> </div>Again, these things are extremely complicated and locals are not just innocent victims either, but yes, Europeans screwed up things too. I'm not against the game talking about these things, but I'm concerned about the &quot;how&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This has been an essential theme of WtA from the beginning. You can't stop murder by killing murderers. You can't stop wars by killing all the soldiers. The Garou are warriors trying to stop things you can't end with violence. Ending them requires understanding the complexity of why things are happening, historical context, and addressing that most of these problems require long term investment to counter regression.<br /> <br /> If all you do is blow up factories, you'll never stop Pentex. You have to understand the systems Pentex exploits to maintain it's profits despite whatever physical damage you inflict on it's subsidiaries. You have to figure out how to alter cultures to remove the demand for Pentex's products. Etc. </div> </div> </div>Again, it's about how you approach these themes and questions, with how much bias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But your examples aren't about this. </div> </div> </div>How they aren't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20 still has the Technocracy as bad fascists and the Traditions as good minority rights activists. </div> </div> </div>No, I put my foot down there, they are not. If you want to read them like that, go ahead. Phill might say that forcing one's will on reality and one's paradigm on the world is facism, but I have problems with that assertion. Also, <i>some</i> traditions might be tied to certain ethnicities, or cultures, but sure as hell they are not minority rights activists. If anything, the Disparate Alliance are more along those lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20 just has the space to be a lot more nuanced and detailed than the Prelude did (not that I disagree that the Prelude is bad for it, and the refugee crisis in particular wasn't a good choice in my mind if you want a more black &amp; white issue for the Ascension warriors to square off over instead of a much more messy and muddy one). </div> </div> </div>In my eyes, there is no black and white issues, really, especially not in Mage and forcing contemporary narratives on it does it a disservice. Even Phill agreed with that on FB.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pandering is really a matter of presentation not the core content. </div> </div> </div>With that, I agree. Though presentation could go that far as altering the core content, thus making it all about the pandering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even then, plenty of pandering is so minor that it's not really a big deal. There's been lots of token minority characters in films that haven't been hurtful to those minorities, or actively made the films worse for anyone that's not racist. It might not be real representation that makes the world more egalitarian, but it doesn't drag media into some inescapable slippery slope either. </div> </div> </div>Except when it does and becomes an all-prevalent thing and thus, a big deal. But of course, it's a matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a pretty big difference between variance in interpretations based on our different backgrounds, and a statement that seems to forget the core and explicitly stated themes of half the Tribes, and that one of the big enemies in the game is Pentex.<br /> <br /> There is no level of good faith reading of WtA that allows for our differences to include, &quot;WtA hasn't always included minority groups fighting corrupt capitalists&quot; as a fair statement about the game. </div> </div> </div>Included. It included tribes being bitter over colinialism and fighting for their kinfloks' people. But the game as whole wasn't centered on just that. <br /> <br /> And the anti-capitalism thing... Werewolf is anti-corporation (or unchecked megacoproration, really), not anti-capitalist. Most of the tribes are happily particiapate in capitalism and werewolf culture is essentially a meritocratic one, to the extremes, where at the same time, we've got Silver Fangs too.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, it had a lot of themes and I fear the narrowing down of those and a more biased presentation, at the end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T18:14:44-07:00","id":1250584,"title":"","content":"Australia. Born and raised in very, very rural South Australia. Just to add another 'exception'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T18:58:35-07:00","id":1250600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250469#post1250469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you know, we might have different reads on things in the game, because of different backgrounds and we might put emphasis in our minds on different things from what we read... I know it's hard to imagine, but trust me, it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to ignore so, so much to make that possible. For starters, large numbers of Garou and Fera aren't white. For another thing, most totems have bans that make living in capitalist society difficult, if not impossible. Some of them also proscribe action against minorities or require that Garou and/or Fera go to their aid. This is on top of how bloated plutocracies resulting from capitalism feed the Wyrm's wayward bits like an all you can eat buffet, often to the tune of fomori.<br /> <br /> And what of the major breeds of fomori? Enticers, Sicklungs, Sons of Typhon, Throwbacks, Normalites, Gorehounds... they're all rather transparent indictments of societies that followed European colonialism. I'm pretty sure those alone cover all the bases of the &quot;everything but vegan&quot; group, but just to top it off, one last mention.<br /> <br /> The Seventh Generation.<br /> <br /> The game has clearly lined up what it regards as evils in need of fighting, and what you described, again, pretty much sums up the list on the human end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T05:52:33-07:00","id":1250720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250581#post1250581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but when you say &quot;institutional and intersectional inequality&quot;, I see it as a certain narrative and talking points more confined to certain places and groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? In English these are things that, like climate change, are a matter of fact for the academics that study them. When the conservative (by the US standards!) majority Supreme Court of the US has made multiple rulings now that acknowledge systemic inequalities the idea that this is a &quot;leftist narrative&quot; is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> There isn't a &quot;both sides&quot; here. There's the facts as we best understand them, and the narratives that try to undermine facts because they're bad for someone's bottom line (or worse reasons, but money seems to hold more power than not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In contrast, lots of the leftist social talking points are much more debated and much more confined. </div> </div> </div>And most &quot;leftist social talking points,&quot; are better known as, &quot;current social science,&quot; that are publicly diminished by the right to claim equity so they can be countered with endless debating rather than solved. It also really shouldn't matter how &quot;confined&quot; something is, especially when it comes to things like human rights. Human rights shouldn't be protected based on meeting minimum population levels before you pay attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, trans rights, problems and issues. It's a very small percent of the population which is actually affected by it. </div> </div> </div>Except it trans rights issues don't actually stop at trans people. When trans rights aren't acknowledged or respected it impacts the families and friends. Trans youth have extremely high homelessness rates, and increases in the homeless population impacts the whole community (having homeless people is actually expensive with the impact it has on public services, it's generally less burdensome on the tax payers to subsidize housing for the homeless than it is to leave them on the streets). Etc<br /> <br /> This is why words like &quot;systemic,&quot; institutional,&quot; and &quot;intersectional,&quot; aren't actually some &quot;leftist narrative.&quot; They're simply acknowledge how social issues don't stop at the neat lines drawn in demographics, and overlapping social issues compound problems in a fashion that's a net negative for everyone if not properly addressed; which is why the climate change analogy works).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying it's unimportant and that we shouldn't try to solve them (though the &quot;how&quot; of solving them is, again, highly debated, as factions can't even agree with the actual problems), but most people aren't affected by them. </div> </div> </div>Every American is affected by anti-trans policies enacted in the US armed services (even if our military is a bloated monster of bureaucracy with an insane budget that should have never been allowed to grow this big) disrupting military readiness while we have troops actively engaged in combat.<br /> <br /> Maybe you should stop conflating &quot;dones't affect people equally,&quot; with, &quot;doesn't affect people at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the main thing is, that the problems in different regions are not the same, as well as the surrounding cultures and as well as how people approach them. </div> </div> </div>And yes, we see problems that transcend cultures, locations, and so on. The solutions might need to be tailored to each place. But when you see black and brown skinned young men significantly over-arrested, over-prosecuted, and over-sentenced in white majority countries separated by an ocean, something is wrong that's not just a local issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, you're an exception, congrats! </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, do you think I'm an exception to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Naturally, stereotypes are not absolute truths, but they usually have an ammount of truth, that's just how it works. </div> </div> </div>That's hardly a sufficient justification for your assertion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thank you, I usually try to see what's going on, instead of buying into narratives and beliefs. </div> </div> </div>Um... you do realize I was being sarcastic there, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why people on either extreme side of politics tend to not like me, because I call bullshit on bigot and senseless righties just as weel as on bigot and senseless leftists. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it has far more to do with you wanting to call bullshit on everyone to feel superior from your &quot;neutral&quot; position rather than making substantive points that pisses people off? Just saying. Not labeling yourself &quot;right&quot; or &quot;left&quot; doesn't mean you're automatically free of your own narratives and bubbles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, it wasn't about ethnic minorities, they're certianly encountering <i>that</i>. It was more about the gender and feminism-related stuff and I have gay individuals and women among them. </div> </div> </div>Seems kinda convenient that you shifted from &quot;PoC and LGBTQ+&quot; to just LGBTQ+ the second you got called out on the PoC part.<br /> <br /> But this fails to see how things are complicated and interconnected. When, to keep on the example, young men of color are over-criminalized, it decreases their ability to economically contribute, putting more economic stress on WoC in those communities (hey, feminist stuff!) as they have to cover the same economic costs as other women who have more support from the men in their ethnic groups, which creates a vicious cycle of reduced wealth, opportunity, and stability leading to more criminal activity, leading to more over-policing, leading to more over-criminalization, repeat. This isn't a &quot;narrative&quot; this is a well studied fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant that certain things are just not widespread problems for most of the population. </div> </div> </div>But you offer no proof besides the majority of the population simply not seeing it as a problem rather than anything to support it not being a problem with much broader impact than people acknowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aaaaand you guys kept dismissing them and kept calling them names and you've got Trump. </div> </div> </div>Right. You serious need to get out of your bubble, because you know jack shit about US politics other than whatever little section of commenters you listen to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, the leftist urban (mostly Budapest) intelligentsia here is doing the same for a long time and we've got the third 2/3 win of Orb\u00e1n this spring. </div> </div> </div>How long of a time could they have been digging this grave? I'm older than the Third Republic, and Orban's been PM for ~1/3 of it (and isn't the only right leaning PM Hungary's had since dropping Communism).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, it's about how you approach these themes and questions, with how much bias. </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with the rather left leaning approach of WtA's current status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How they aren't? </div> </div> </div>I explained my position in the rest of the paragraph so you didn't have to ask.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I put my foot down there, they are not. </div> </div> </div>What's your argumentation other than, &quot;I don't like to read them that way?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, <i>some</i> traditions might be tied to certain ethnicities, or cultures, but sure as hell they are not minority rights activists. If anything, the Disparate Alliance are more along those lines. </div> </div> </div>1) By necessity the Traditions all have minority rights activists in their numbers, because they all support groups that are minorities, even if no single Tradition is a universal minority right's activist group. The Traditions as a whole are explicitly a minority rights activist group by their founding principles. The Resolution of Intent directly committed all the member Traditions to mutual defense of each other and their cultural practices.<br /> <br /> 2) The Traditions and the Disparate Alliance can both be so without contradiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my eyes, there is no black and white issues, really, especially not in Mage and forcing contemporary narratives on it does it a disservice. Even Phill agreed with that on FB. </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're conflating things and misrepresenting Satyros there. There are absolutely black and white issues in Mage, he's responsible for writing in a few of them. And he also wrote a bunch of contemporary narratives into the game. Trying to twist the black and white stuff to fit contemporary narratives (like &quot;Trump supporters are all Nephandi or Nephandi dupes!&quot;) is clearly not good, but there's two different issues here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except when it does and becomes an all-prevalent thing and thus, a big deal. </div> </div> </div>Right, and we're really not in any danger of that happening any time soon... so seems weird to worry about it for W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the game as whole wasn't centered on just that. </div> </div> </div>You can't have seven Tribes focused on human minorities, another Tribe focused on a historically mistreated ethnic group that was in the middle of a major struggle when first developed, and another Tribe focused on persecution of animals... so 9/13 of the Tribes have this as something they're fighting against, plus the remaining four (and the other half of the Fianna being a borderline case in the first group) all still have this as a theme going in the opposite direction (ex: the Fenrir and sexism). They game has always had this as one (yes not the only) central thematic elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the anti-capitalism thing... Werewolf is anti-corporation (or unchecked megacoproration, really), not anti-capitalist. Most of the tribes are happily particiapate in capitalism and werewolf culture is essentially a meritocratic one, to the extremes, where at the same time, we've got Silver Fangs too. </div> </div> </div>Capitalism is explicitly a Weaver element, and only wholly embraced by... the Glass Walkers because they're the pro-Weaver Tribe. None of the other Tribes &quot;happily&quot; participate in capitalism, they just don't have much of a choice if they're going to participate in mainstream human society (which a good number of them don't advocate doing much of anyway). The Silver Fangs especially aren't capitalists, because that takes power away from royalty, as well as capitalism not being a system that rewards merit, but rewards pre-existing economic advantages earned or unearned.<br /> <br /> Plus all the stuff Saur Ops beat me to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the thing, it had a lot of themes and I fear the narrowing down of those and a more biased presentation, at the end. </div> </div> </div>Eh. WtA has a lot of themes, but the whole &quot;Captain Planet&quot; criticism is based on how little it explores most of them for the culture warrior eco-terrorists fighting capitalism its military industrial complex to be the dominant narrative of the game anyway. Part of the whole problem with the WoD (at least pre-V5 and we'll see how that goes) is that the End Times Are Nigh, which makes a lot of the themes irrelevant because they'd take too long to explore in-game before the Apocalypse happens unless you ignore that in your personal games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T09:05:00-07:00","id":1250766,"title":"","content":"I'll add my bits here and there<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Werewolf is not a game that play just against corporate capitalism, is a game that goes against capitalism in general. You could say that the main theme of the game is the fight against what in econ are called &quot;externalities&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Externality\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Externality\" target=\"_blank\"> Externality - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Externality\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Externality </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There is no market solution that will internalize all externalities. Consequently, elements of the moral economy must be used, including social norms, law, leadership, and hierarchy. &quot;All of these structures are grounded in trust, which when supplemented with sanctions, can be used to generate complex institutional forms that can sustain outcomes that are not strategic equilibria.&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>2) Capitalism will always become corporate capitalism. While perfect competition is the standard assumption in economic modelling the most widespread markets you will find are either oligopoly or monopoly. Perfect competition is a useful conceptual tool since it allows to create a &quot;standard&quot; situation and then figure how the variations of it work.<br /> But capitalism will mostly always evolve into corporate capitalism for the following factors<br /> <br /> <br /> A) Economies of scale<br /> <br /> B) Economies of scope<br /> <br /> C) Better risk allocation (this is especially true for the bank sector, bigger banks can deal with more risk)<br /> <br /> D) High sunk cost<br /> <br /> E) Patent laws.<br /> <br /> Even Daron Acemoglu (which is relly not &quot;left-wing&quot;), MIT professor, one of the most important and influential academics in the world (is among the top 10 economist for level of citations in academic papers), said that market power become political power at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Economic power tends to beget political power even in democratic and pluralistic societies. In the United States, this tends to work through campaign contributions and access to politicians that wealth and money tend to buy. This political channel implies another, potentially more powerful and distortionary link between inequality and a non-level playing field. It may also create pathways from inequality to instability, because both the economic and political implications of inequality can create various backlashes.</i></span></span> </div> </div> </div>3) Capitalism is not meritocratic (there is no such thing as meritrocracy in the world, no system is ever truly &quot;meritocratic&quot;).<br /> <br /> The most part of your future revenue is dictated by who was your father and where are you from, merit is...a lesser commodity<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.ft.com/content/8001d074-dcc9-11e6-86ac-f253db7791c6\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ft.com/content/8001d074-dcc9-11e6-86ac-f253db7791c6<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.ft.com/__origami/service/image/v2/images/raw/http%3A%2F%2Fcom.ft.imagepublish.prod.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68174a1c-f929-11e6-9516-2d969e0d3b65?source=next&amp;fit=scale-down&amp;width=600\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Investment managers from low-income backgrounds consistently achieve better results for their clients than colleagues from affluent backgrounds, according to a December 2016 study by the National Bureau of Economic Research in the US.<br /> Because individuals from less-privileged backgrounds faced a greater number of obstacles to reaching prestigious positions, the NBER researchers found \u201conly the most skilled\u201d succeeded in getting a foothold in the first place. The study looked at fund managers who had got into the elevated position of running a fund, however. Often, people from less wealthy backgrounds never make it this far, the researchers found, saying \u201cthose born poor are promoted only if they outperform\u201d. John Craven, a former derivatives banker, believes class determines promotion. He quit his job in 2012 to become a teacher. While he did well in sales, he believes the City is riven with social prejudice when it comes to client-facing roles. Many firms have a strong discourse of meritocracy, but as you attempt to climb the pyramid, you see it isn\u2019t true The top roles in banking tend to involve revenue generation, he says. So managers assume employees who have more in common with clients will be better at making money. They will be given clients likely to do the most business with the bank. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.ft.com/content/af1f01be-1564-11e7-b0c1-37e417ee6c76\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ft.com/content/af1f01be-...1-37e417ee6c76</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cChildren from high-income backgrounds who show signs of low academic ability at age five are 35 per cent more likely to become high earners than their poorer peers who show early signs of high ability,\u201d the education secretary told a conference on social mobility on Thursday.<br /> She added that even when academic achievements are similar, pupils from more wealthy backgrounds tend to earn more. \u201c<br /> Graduates from disadvantaged backgrounds who do make it to the top jobs still earn, on average, over \u00a32,200 a year less than their colleagues who happen to have been born to professional or managerial parents, even when they have the same educational attainment, the same role and the same experience,\u201d she said. Ms Greening was the first in her family to go to university \u201cI\u2019m not someone who ever planned to go into politics,\u201d she said. \u201cFar from it. Actually, some of my earliest memories of politicians are of my father shouting at politicians who turned up on the news, frustrated that he felt they didn\u2019t really talk about his life.\u201d Sir Peter Lampl, founder of the social mobility charity the Sutton Trust, said Ms Greening was right to highlight the \u201ctragic waste of talent that blights the UK\u201d. \u201cMany young people from low and moderate income backgrounds lack essential life skills such as confidence, articulacy and social skills,\u201d he said. \u201cThe state system needs to do a better job of equipping youngsters with these skills, which are essential for success in life.\u201d </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-02-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T09:22:19-07:00","id":1250774,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250720#post1250720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And most &quot;leftist social talking points,&quot; are better known as, &quot;current social science,&quot; that are publicly diminished by the right to claim equity so they can be countered with endless debating rather than solved. It also really shouldn't matter how &quot;confined&quot; something is, especially when it comes to things like human rights. Human rights shouldn't be protected based on meeting minimum population levels before you pay attention.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I want to emphasize this point.<br /> <br /> There is no thing as leftist social talking points, there is the current state of art of social sciences, which is accepted in most of the western liberal world.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the state of art concerning Trans-gender's and their well-beign after transition, directly from the database of the Cornell University.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whatweknow.inequality.cornell.edu/topics/lgbt-equality/what-does-the-scholarly-research-say-about-the-well-being-of-transgender-people/\" target=\"_blank\">https://whatweknow.inequality.cornel...gender-people/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">And this is on another hot theme like homosexual parents.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whatweknow.inequality.cornell.edu/topics/lgbt-equality/what-does-the-scholarly-research-say-about-the-wellbeing-of-children-with-gay-or-lesbian-parents/\" target=\"_blank\">https://whatweknow.inequality.cornel...sbian-parents/</a></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a very important point: in these matters there is no thing as &quot;opinions&quot;, there is only what social science discovered and researched in the last 30 years and has become the scientific consensus.<br /> <br /> Do this people suffer discrimination?<br /> <br /> Yeah they do<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/06/16/us/hate-crimes-against-lgbt.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/...inst-lgbt.html</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Nearly a fifth of the 5,462 so-called single-bias hate crimes <a href=\"https://www.fbi.gov/news/stories/2015/november/latest-hate-crime-statistics-available\" target=\"_blank\">reported to the F.B.I.</a> in 2014 were because of the target\u2019s sexual orientation, or, in some cases, their perceived orientation.</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Ironically, part of the reason for violence against L.G.B.T. people might have to do with a more accepting attitude toward gays and lesbians in recent decades, say people who study hate crimes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">As the majority of society becomes more tolerant of L.G.B.T. people, some of those who are opposed to them become more radical, said Mark Potok, a senior fellow at the Southern Poverty Law Center.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The flip side of marriage equality is that people who strongly oppose it find the shifting culture extremely disturbing, said Gregory M. Herek, a psychology professor at the University of California, Davis, who is an expert on anti-gay violence.</span></span></span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><b>For Many Reasons, Hate<br /> Crimes Are Underreported</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Finding accurate statistics about hate crimes targeting L.G.B.T. people is challenging, in part, because victims \u2014 fearful of outing themselves to family members or employers \u2014 might choose not to report an attack, Mr. Herek said.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">A recent report by the <a href=\"http://www.bjs.gov/content/pub/pdf/hcv0412st.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Bureau of Justice Statistics</a> found that most crimes are not reported to the police, and those that are reported are frequently not classified as hate crimes by local jurisdictions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">A recent investigation by <a href=\"http://bigstory.ap.org/article/8247a1d2f76b4baea2a121186dedf768/ap-patchy-reporting-undercuts-national-hate-crimes-count\" target=\"_blank\">The Associated Press</a> found that thousands of city police and county sheriff\u2019s departments had not filed a single hate crime report to the F.B.I. between 2009 and 2014.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Larger cities or cities with a more visible L.G.B.T. community are more likely to have procedures and training in place to detect and reduce hate crimes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">For example, in 2014 only one hate crime was reported for the entire state of Mississippi. In Connecticut, where L.G.B.T. people are arguably more visible and influential, 23 hate crimes based on sexual orientation were reported, Mr. Herek said.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Minority Transgender<br /> Women Are Frequent Targets</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">A look at four years of homicides of L.G.B.T. people catalogued by the <a href=\"http://www.avp.org/resources/reports/term/summary\" target=\"_blank\">National Coalition of Anti-Violence Programs</a> shows that the vast majority of those who were killed were black or Hispanic transgender people.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><img src=\"https://static01.nyt.com/newsgraphics/2016/06/13/lgbt-hatecrime/cc60b64b4f28cecefc35856c3c8052c5990a959b/hatecrime_murder_race-Artboard_1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">L.G.B.T. homicides by race and sexuality</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">2012-2015</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">8</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">39</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">11</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">11</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">19</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Black</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">transgender women</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Black</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">gay men</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">White</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">gay men</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Latino</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">transgender</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">women</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Other</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><img src=\"https://static01.nyt.com/newsgraphics/2016/06/13/lgbt-hatecrime/cc60b64b4f28cecefc35856c3c8052c5990a959b/hatecrime_murder_type-Artboard_1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">L.G.B.T. homicides by type of attacks</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">2012-2015</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">13</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">47</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">13</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Shooting</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stabbing</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Beating</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-franklin\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Source: National Coalition of Anti-Violence Programs</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">The group collects data on violence against L.G.B.T. people in 12 states, and is considered one of the most authoritative sources of such data.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">It recorded 88 homicides of L.G.B.T. people from 2012 to 2015. The data offers insight into the victims of extreme violence, but the total number L.G.B.T. homicides is most likely much higher since the group is not able to collect data nationwide.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Among those killed last year was <a href=\"http://www.nbcnews.com/news/nbcblk/india-clarke-10th-trans-woman-killed-year-n397451\" target=\"_blank\">India Clarke</a>, a black transgender woman who was beaten and shot in July in Tampa, Florida. <a href=\"http://www.tampabay.com/news/publicsafety/crime/shooter-accused-of-murdering-tampa-transgender-woman-now-linked-to-second/2241440\" target=\"_blank\">Keith Gaillard</a>, the man charged in her murder, was also accused of killing a man believed to be gay less than a week later.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">A separate report by the <a href=\"http://hrc-assets.s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com//files/assets/resources/HRC-AntiTransgenderViolence-0519.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Human Rights Campaign</a> said that more transgender people were killed in 2015 than during any other year on record.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">At a time when transgender people are gaining visibility, \u201ctransgender women of color are facing an epidemic of violence that occurs at the intersections of racism, sexism and transphobia \u2013 issues that advocates can no longer afford to address separately,\u201d Chad Griffin, the president of the Human Rights Campaign, said in the report.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">There is a long history, particularly in the transgender community, of not being treated with respect by law enforcement, social service agencies and the legal system, said Roger Coggan, director of legal services at the Los Angeles L.G.B.T. Center.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:nyt-cheltenham\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">\u201cUnfortunately, we just have to accept the fact that stigma based on sexual orientation is still widespread,\u201d Mr. Herek said. \u201cOvercoming those prejudices is a lot of work.\u201d</span></span></span></span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/news/press-releases/gay-men-and-lesbians-violent-events-and-subsequent-ptsd/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://hsph.harvard.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Social-Share@2x-1024x538.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/news/press-releases/gay-men-and-lesbians-violent-events-and-subsequent-ptsd/\" target=\"_blank\"> News | Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/news/press-releases/gay-men-and-lesbians-violent-events-and-subsequent-ptsd/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/news/press-releases/gay-men-and-lesbians-violent-events-and-subsequent-ptsd/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The latest public health news delivered right to your inbox. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#595859\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Boston, MA \u2013 A new study from researchers at the Harvard School of Public Health (HSPH) and Children\u2019s Hospital Boston has found that gay men, lesbians, bisexuals, and heterosexuals who have ever had a same-sex sex partner are one-and-a-half to two times as likely to experience violent events, especially in childhood, than the general population and have double the risk of experiencing posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) as a consequence of these events. It is the first study to directly link higher rates of PTSD in those four groups (classified as sexual minorities) to greater violence exposure.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> So no, there is no such things as &quot;opinions&quot; in this field: there are the facts, hard facts cemented by years of research and data.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-02-2018, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T03:39:26-07:00","id":1251011,"title":"","content":"This is why sociology and associated subjects are derided by so many; they don't like the results of certain enquiries so they frame the whole endeavour as bunk (until a sociological study can be poorly interpreted to blame immigrants for something complicated; obviously sociology is suddenly good if it gives results that I like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T05:02:21-07:00","id":1251024,"title":"","content":"I don't want to go into detail on the LGBT discussion. Iirc the LGBT community is estimated by 4.5% and whether that is significantly represented in media or not is a whole other topic.<br /> <br /> For WtA I hope that it is made clear, that &quot;garou shall not mate with garou&quot; is forbidding any romantic relationship between any garou, period. And, that the tenet exists so that the garou would need to have relationships with their Kin, and not separate themselves from those they should protect any further...<br /> <br /> That said, the percentage of LGBT in the supernatural population should match that of the human population, and there is nothing that should affect this. Garou regeneration could be a bad thing for transgender, but if W5, or any rulebook really needs to address that, is whole other question.<br /> <br /> But in general, I find that the W5 books shouldn't make an effort to forcefully include any minority the authors can find. I'm thinking of the Anui prople and their Uktena connection. I felt it wasn't really necessary to have Uktena in Japan, and why the Hakken hadn't kicked them out of their territory ages ago.<br /> <br /> Also, if a Player wants to play a person from a minority, they shouldn't be limited in their character options, because a author made a connection to one specific tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T07:55:38-07:00","id":1251067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251024#post1251024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in general, I find that the W5 books shouldn't make an effort to forcefully include any minority the authors can find. I'm thinking of the Anui prople and their Uktena connection. I felt it wasn't really necessary to have Uktena in Japan, and why the Hakken hadn't kicked them out of their territory ages ago.<br /> <br /> Also, if a Player wants to play a person from a minority, they shouldn't be limited in their character options, because a author made a connection to one specific tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have the whole Ainu thing backwards. People possibly will play more of them, if they are tied to a certain tribe. I mean, how common are ainu characters in your games? XD<br /> <br /> Aside from that, forcefully including them is hardly what is happening. Uktena have been stated to include groups that try to keep to their ways despite oppression and ainu fit that to a tee. As do sami or any russian people. WtA has always been a game that thrives on discussing minority rights, so including lesser known people to the table is not forcing it. It is showcasing them to people who wouldn't otherwise even know about them.<br /> <br /> Forcing it would be if Finnish garou were all suddenly Glass Walkers, because Finnish (city) people love technology and invent new things fast. The connection would be just a quick throw-away, rather than fitting into the MO of a tribe. Or that all of Finland was just a huge Black Spiral Hive. It wouldn't do anything to the setting, because it would just take away from the available concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T08:11:35-07:00","id":1251070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251024#post1251024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if a Player wants to play a person from a minority, they shouldn't be limited in their character options, because a author made a connection to one specific tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this has happened however. Werewolf books have made it clear that certain tribes have a certain ethnicity more frequently on average, along with certain Fera breeds. Your average Werelion will have African heritage. But Werewolf lore also makes it clear that these are just trends, and that there won't always be this ethnic link. You can play a Hispanic person and play any Tribe or Breed you like, it will just be more or less common in different groups. And you can easily hand-wave it by pointing out that many Garou/Fera will have offspring with people outside of the common ethnicity for their tribe or breed.<br /> <br /> I do think that these groupings will influence people's decisions however; for example, I would guess that most Native American Mage PCs are going to be in Shamanic Crafts and Traditions linked to the Native Americans; very few people will play a Native American Void Engineer or Hermetic, and that's a shame really. So I think a sidebar in books saying &quot;Yeah most of this splat (Tribe, Tradition, Breed, Clan, Bloodline) are X (native american, asian, men, women), but feel free to do something else.&quot; This should apply to most splats, with a few exceptions of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T09:00:29-07:00","id":1251077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251070#post1251070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that these groupings will influence people's decisions however; for example, I would guess that most Native American Mage PCs are going to be in Shamanic Crafts and Traditions linked to the Native Americans; very few people will play a Native American Void Engineer or Hermetic, and that's a shame really. So I think a sidebar in books saying &quot;Yeah most of this splat (Tribe, Tradition, Breed, Clan, Bloodline) are X (native american, asian, men, women), but feel free to do something else.&quot; This should apply to most splats, with a few exceptions of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true, it is also something I wish people would feel brave doing. Yes, your culture influences a lot from you, especially cultures under threat like the First Nations people. But that isn't all they are. Some might even on purpose reject it.<br /> <br /> I still love my ronin theurge with PB5 wendigo (looks, none of the oomph.) He is more scientific minded than spontaneous and his faith has a christian bend to it. But that doesn't magically take away the racism he faces and the assumptions people make of him. He faces the exact same crap that he would if he had been raised in his native culture, but he lacks the support network he would have had if he had been raised in his culture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T09:18:34-07:00","id":1251078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251077#post1251077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very true, it is also something I wish people would feel brave doing. Yes, your culture influences a lot from you, especially cultures under threat like the First Nations people. But that isn't all they are. Some might even on purpose reject it.<br /> <br /> I still love my ronin theurge with PB5 wendigo (looks, none of the oomph.) He is more scientific minded than spontaneous and his faith has a christian bend to it. But that doesn't magically take away the racism he faces and the assumptions people make of him. He faces the exact same crap that he would if he had been raised in his native culture, but he lacks the support network he would have had if he had been raised in his culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find stories about Ronin very interesting. I had a concept for a sort of &quot;Suicide Squad&quot; game where all of the PCs were stray supernaturals who ended up being the useful servants of a generous patron, some Ventrue Elder. They included a Ronin who was abandoned by his family, and after the first change attempted to join two tribes and was rejected by both (socially in one case, and in the ritual in another). Completely betrayed by society and the Garou Nation in his view, homeless and alone, his life changed when a Ventrue who requires the blood of homeless people tried to feed from him. He fled in the form of a wolf, leaving a stunned Neonate. This story spread to their Grandsire, who approached and seduced the Ronin using Presence, giving them affection and support and maternal/paternal love for the first time in their life. This would be a deeply uncomfortable and... controversial backstory for a player character, and the ST would do well to keep focus on the fact that you have a Vampire who is several hundred years old forming a semi-romantic bond with a 17 year old who is vulnerable and incredibly useful to them. That the bond is legitimate, but incredibly... problematic. That the interaction is incredibly unequal and has some subtly abusive elements, but that the Ronin would be the first to defend it.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've been rejected my whole life. S/He was the first person to ever care about who I was, to give me a place to stay, to give me some kind of purpose. And you're going to preach to me about how wrong it is, call me a traitor? I was betrayed by my own blood, twice. Abandoned three times. They care about me, and the Garou never did. Of course a powerful person pulling you into a world of mystery and excitement, giving you a fight to win, jobs to do, that's just TERRIBLE. And I suppose that hasn't happened to any of you? Fucking hypocrites. Get out before I call for security.&quot;<br /> <br /> The other ideas for members I had were a psychic fomorus who was sold to the Ventrue after a branch of Pentex collapsed, a Dhampir searching for their thin-blooded parent, that sort of thing. The idea was that the Elder wanted to have servants with serious needs which could only be fulfilled by someone with powerful connections (access to a drug developed by that defunct Pentex subsidiary, information about a thin-blood that died years ago), and who also would have unusual supernatural abilities that his enemies would be unable to predict or defend against. People are used to ghouls of course, but a rogue werewolf and a potent possessed psychic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-03-2018, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:50:34-07:00","id":1251375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251067#post1251067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have the whole Ainu thing backwards. People possibly will play more of them, if they are tied to a certain tribe. I mean, how common are ainu characters in your games? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>None. <br /> <br /> In 1st/2nd Edition the Uktena were described as having made the decision (at a grand moot) to integrate minorities that came to their historical territory (parts of North America) to their tribe's kin and therefore integrate their culture into the tribe to some degree. That is different from traveling to other countries, seeking out minorities and settling with them. One is a tribe choosing compromise to survive, the other is a tribe seeking to expand it's territory beyond their historical home land.<br /> <br /> But, even with that change, there is a difference between writing &quot;the Uktena are settling wit the Ainu&quot; and &quot;There are Uktena seeking out people, that are a minority within the areas or political states they live in and try to integrate with them to expand their territory and influence world wide. If you would like to play such a character, you might be interested to read up on the Ainu in Japan, or minorities in Russia or...:&quot;<br /> <br /> The way it is presented is, in my opinion, forcing new aspects into the Setting, rather than provide an option.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T09:09:42-07:00","id":1251404,"title":"","content":"Redundancy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-04-2018, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T09:37:48-07:00","id":1251417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250600#post1250600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd have to ignore so, so much to make that possible. For starters, large numbers of Garou and Fera aren't white.</div> </div> </div> </div>And?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For another thing, most totems have bans that make living in capitalist society difficult, if not impossible. </div> </div> </div>Re-read the W20 corebook totem descritpions. You're speaking nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of them also proscribe action against minorities or require that Garou and/or Fera go to their aid. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Wendigo. The one Tribe that is openly racist and even the Uktenas say is taking things too far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is on top of how bloated plutocracies resulting from capitalism feed the Wyrm's wayward bits like an all you can eat buffet, often to the tune of fomori. </div> </div> </div>Have you ever lived in a post-socialist country? I assure you there's plenty of Wyrm-feeding stuff in those, nevermind actual communist ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what of the major breeds of fomori? Enticers, Sicklungs, Sons of Typhon, Throwbacks, Normalites, Gorehounds... they're all rather transparent indictments of societies that followed European colonialism. I'm pretty sure those alone cover all the bases of the &quot;everything but vegan&quot; group, but just to top it off, one last mention.<br /> <br /> The Seventh Generation.<br /> <br /> The game has clearly lined up what it regards as evils in need of fighting, and what you described, again, pretty much sums up the list on the human end.<br /> </div> </div> </div>For one, you have an interesting worldview, if you think the things those types of Fomori represent are unique to post-colonialism society.<br /> <br /> But, what is the more important: you're confusing my problems with the game's themes of corruption in general and the portrayal of it (which I don't have problems with) with my wariness of the game framing them in a certain kind of narrative in the future. <br /> <br /> That's why I've said we look upon these things with different eyes. You choose to interpret these things in a way that is different from mine, because our surrounding culture and experiences are different too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T11:55:24-07:00","id":1251451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251417#post1251417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And?</div> </div> </div> </div>And that means that, going by that, it's going to be a POC-led affair in a lot of cases. Oddly enough, this also holds true for the Red Talons; if you're going by their Homid appearance by the watchwords of &quot;looks like early humans&quot;, then they aren't going to be white, because pale skin is a very recent thing in humanity (only becoming commonplace in the last six thousand years). Any game that concentrates on Fera is also going to have a tiny number of white people present, because Fera were usually written as not being white.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Re-read the W20 corebook totem descritpions. You're speaking nonsense. </div> </div> </div>Sure. We'll go down the list in order of appearance.<br /> <br /> Falcon: You can't dishonor the totem or lose permanent Honor. Given the Renown Chart's outline of Honor, this means that you have to drop what you're doing and help the helpless. If, like in the Incredibles, your boss is lecturing you about the importance of not standing out while you see a mugging happen, you have to walk out to do something, because if you keep ignoring them, that might be the straw that breaks the camel's back with your permanent Honor dots. Jobs are also quite heavy on circumstances where you might endanger the veil (big-time Honor hit, there), so the smart choice would be not to have one.<br /> <br /> Grandfather Thunder: Can't entertain sycophants. While this totem is more conducive to living in a high place and looking down on people, it is a very particular form of it, and companies that followers of Grandfather Thunder run are going to be weird in comparison to the others. And they will run them; their totem wouldn't come to them if they weren't preoccupied with getting on top of things. Whether or not this pans out is another matter entirely; in any case, witnessing the climb up is going to make existing management very uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Pegasus: Cannot refuse to help women, particularly young women. In practice, this means picking fights with most of management and HR on a regular basis, especially when dealing with missing stairs.<br /> <br /> Stag: Have to drop everything to aid fae, which are typically not well-disposed to corporate enterprise. Also, must respect prey ceremonially, which means good luck dealing with the food industry.<br /> <br /> Bear: Bear doesn't ask anything of packs, but it seems like it would go against Bear's general nature to not offer Succor like Gurahl.<br /> <br /> Boar: Has the same problem as Stag not knowing where food comes from.<br /> <br /> Fenris: You will not be popular with your boss, much like how Goku or Vegeta would not be.<br /> <br /> Griffin: Doesn't associate with humans, but savvy Red Talons might realize that it could pay off to kill the oppressors in control of everything first and then see how things pan out from there, if only because it's less exposure and effort to have a surgical strike.<br /> <br /> Rat: Can't kill vermin; the expansion in the Bone Gnawers tribebook and Ratkin also note that Rat Mother followers typically spend a great deal of their time aiding the homeless, while followers of the Rat God want to tear down Weaver-ridden capitalist industrial society.<br /> <br /> Wendigo we already covered.<br /> <br /> Chimera: Good luck finding enlightenment in banal paperwork and office politics.<br /> <br /> Cockroach: Never killing a cockroach runs into a bit of the same problem as Rat never killing rats. The health inspector will not like you, and neither will anyone else who knows about your cockroach pit.<br /> <br /> Owl: Requires frequent trips to the wilderness to offer up restrained rodents or other prey items for owls. In the WoD, this is going to be one hell of a commute, since the dark, spooky woods are typically rather a long drive out from the massive cities.<br /> <br /> Raven: Can't carry around wealth.<br /> <br /> Uktena: Your full-time job is going to be recovering important information and objects from the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Unicorn: Must protect and aid the weak and exploited. Capitalism thrives on making people weak and exploited in the first place, so this is safely a no-go.<br /> <br /> Coyote: Would only be in it to take down structures trying to hem them in.<br /> <br /> Cuckoo: Might be amenable to it, since it wants the pack to improve its standing at the expense of others. Still only a maybe.<br /> <br /> Fox: Fox hunts might be a thing of the past, but modern attempts to trap and kill aren't.<br /> <br /> This is aside from Chiminage that Garou and Fera need to deal with spirits, particularly when learning Gifts. Cuckoo-spirits, incidentally, have much more onerous chiminage than bans, as they forbid attacking birds that aren't corrupted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, Wendigo. The one Tribe that is openly racist and even the Uktenas say is taking things too far. </div> </div> </div>Uh, no, the Wendigo are not racist. They don't control the systemic means of oppression, so it'd be really, really difficult to be that way. They don't like white people, sure, but there's just cause for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever lived in a post-socialist country? I assure you there's plenty of Wyrm-feeding stuff in those, nevermind actual communist ones. </div> </div> </div>The ones nearby you are also post-Stalinist countries, right? That's probably going to be the more important factor. Also, the writings of Marx still had a paternalistic colonial influence running strong, as if I recall correctly communism regarded traditional economies as &quot;proto-communist&quot; and in need of the strong hand of Europe to bring into true fruition. Socialism, incidentally, was not something that I was pushing for; traditional economies were.<br /> <br /> (Rage Across Russia is one of the earliest books that I got for W:tA, in the form of RAtW Volume 1. Socialism has been thoroughly razzed on by W:tA as well, but it's also fallen by the wayside in favor of capitalist economies.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one, you have an interesting worldview, if you think the things those types of Fomori represent are unique to post-colonialism society. </div> </div> </div>They rely very heavily on factors of colonial thinking. The images that they're cut from are exaggerations of European-ness, particularly WASP-ness for the US, as well as fragility of identity. While other locations might manage the industrial scale component, that's going to result in a different expression of mass-produced monsters.<br /> <br /> Also, you didn't address the Seventh Generation. It is literally a bunch of old white guys divided in influence across major parts of society, which originated in Europe but moved to NY, NY.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, what is the more important: you're confusing my problems with the game's themes of corruption in general and the portrayal of it (which I don't have problems with) with my wariness of the game framing them in a certain kind of narrative in the future.<br /> <br /> That's why I've said we look upon these things with different eyes. You choose to interpret these things in a way that is different from mine, because our surrounding culture and experiences are different too. </div> </div> </div>As I noted above, the game as written is concerned with corruption in other places and systems of economics, but the big one today is in how industrialized capitalism is gaining even more influence over governmental process and rarely experiences consequences for their actions. Often, corporate enterprise is also tied into making people feel afraid of a perceived &quot;other&quot; to distract everyone from how a few people are getting rich beyond comprehension at the expense of nearly everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:11:34-07:00","id":1251457,"title":"","content":"Before any response, I want to make it clear that I don't have endless hours to put into these arguments with you, or anyone else and they are not exceptionally productive either, so I won't, after this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1250720#post1250720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on what? In English these are things that, like climate change, are a matter of fact for the academics that study them. When the conservative (by the US standards!) majority Supreme Court of the US has made multiple rulings now that acknowledge systemic inequalities the idea that this is a &quot;leftist narrative&quot; is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert on US Supreme Court ruling, so if you have any links to those rulings that acknowledge sytemic inequalities <i>in a way intersectionalist social justice activists use them now</i>, I'd be happy to read them and re-examine my stance on things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There isn't a &quot;both sides&quot; here. There's the facts as we best understand them, and the narratives that try to undermine facts because they're bad for someone's bottom line (or worse reasons, but money seems to hold more power than not).<br /> <br /> <br /> And most &quot;leftist social talking points,&quot; are better known as, &quot;current social science,&quot; that are publicly diminished by the right to claim equity so they can be countered with endless debating rather than solved. </div> </div> </div>You're omitting the fact that the leftist narrative points weren't just debated by the right, but by academics from a wide variety of political leanings. They just, you know, are not members of a certain tribe, with a certain narrative, so don't share the narrative over certain topics. Not the <i>existence</i> of those topics, but the narrative over them and the conclusions drawn from them by a sub-culture of academicals.<br /> <br /> Also, sociology, as any socilogist would tell you, who worth her degree, is not a hard science, thus the debating. That a part of academia handles several things as ultimate thruths is one of the main problems, as I see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also really shouldn't matter how &quot;confined&quot; something is, especially when it comes to things like human rights. Human rights shouldn't be protected based on meeting minimum population levels before you pay attention. </div> </div> </div>Are you arguing with what, exactly? How we've got here, you making statements about the obvious? Of course, human rights are important. On the other hand, what is and isn't a <i>human right</i> is also a field of debate over several topics, but I won't go into that, just thought it worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> <br /> But honestly, I'm struggling to build up the logical chain that brought us here, as you're pretty good at derailing. What all of this has to do with me not wanting the game's themes being framed in a certain narrative? When I refuted the importance of human rights?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except it trans rights issues don't actually stop at trans people. When trans rights aren't acknowledged or respected it impacts the families and friends. Trans youth have extremely high homelessness rates, and increases in the homeless population impacts the whole community (having homeless people is actually expensive with the impact it has on public services, it's generally less burdensome on the tax payers to subsidize housing for the homeless than it is to leave them on the streets). Etc </div> </div> </div>You seriously think the problems of trans people is having a big impact on homelesness? In comparison to bad loans, unemployement and alcoholism? You're wahsing together two separate things.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm not sayin the plights of transpeople are not important and that we should ignore them. I just said, at the beginning, that several of the leftist talking points are a lot more confined than, say, climate change, in answer to you saying, in reaction to my initial post, that we can't have the themes of Werewolf, without pandering to contemporary leftist narratives. Or you don't get my point, or I don't get your point, or we seriously miscommunicating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why words like &quot;systemic,&quot; institutional,&quot; and &quot;intersectional,&quot; aren't actually some &quot;leftist narrative.&quot; They're simply acknowledge how social issues don't stop at the neat lines drawn in demographics, and overlapping social issues compound problems in a fashion that's a net negative for everyone if not properly addressed; which is why the climate change analogy works). </div> </div> </div>The devil is in the details. It's not the words themselves that are debated, nor the idea that yeah, things add up and overlap. The conclusions drawn by some people and stratas of academia and activism are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every American is affected by anti-trans policies enacted in the US armed services (even if our military is a bloated monster of bureaucracy with an insane budget that should have never been allowed to grow this big) disrupting military readiness while we have troops actively engaged in combat. </div> </div> </div>If we could just have problems this serious and over-reaching in the Hungarian military as well.<br /> <br /> Again, just to be eprfectly-perfectly clear: I'm not saying it's a non-issue, your government and miliary should sort this out. If for no other reason, because it's an important issue for the people involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you should stop conflating &quot;dones't affect people equally,&quot; with, &quot;doesn't affect people at all.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should stop misrepresenting what I've said. Though I could have been more clear, but I tought I was. My bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, we see problems that transcend cultures, locations, and so on. The solutions might need to be tailored to each place. But when you see black and brown skinned young men significantly over-arrested, over-prosecuted, and over-sentenced in white majority countries separated by an ocean, something is wrong that's not just a local issue. </div> </div> </div>That's a criminally oversimplified take on it. Even, <i>even</i> if I can say that yes, most countries have problems with the different majority and minority groups living together, the actual problems, their roots and the possible solutions are wildly different.<br /> <br /> That's one of the biggest crimes of any extremist ideology, really, trying to apply an overarching narrative to differing situations. Usually by pointing out 'the enemy', on which you can blame all of your strifes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What, exactly, do you think I'm an exception to? </div> </div> </div>What do you feel you're an exception to?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's hardly a sufficient justification for your assertion. </div> </div> </div>My assertion of? That the leftist intellectuals of very cosmopolitan areas over the world are seriously out of touch with thei countrymen in rural areas? I'm standing by that. You've said it's a stereotype, I assume, that all American leftists are from Coastal urban regions. Of course it is a stereotype and thus, not exclusively true. But it has truth to it and it's useful, because it highlights a trend, as lots of stereotypes do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um... you do realize I was being sarcastic there, right? </div> </div> </div>Anecdotal evidence about where you live to invalidate an argument about a trend is sarcasm for you? Well, okay, then, I was tired, I must ahve missed it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps it has far more to do with you wanting to call bullshit on everyone to feel superior from your &quot;neutral&quot; position rather than making substantive points that pisses people off? Just saying. </div> </div> </div>Hard to make substantive points in the face of unqestioned beliefs and diagreeing with beliefs that consists a big part of someone's identity is usually what pisses people off. But I assure you, I rarely think I'm superior, because I realize someone is talking nonsense. Mostly it's despairing. Or amusing. Depends on my mood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not labeling yourself &quot;right&quot; or &quot;left&quot; doesn't mean you're automatically free of your own narratives and bubbles. </div> </div> </div>'course not. That's why I'm willing to listen to people actually wanting and be able to discuss things politely and in a collected way. I have little patience for either preaching or histerics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems kinda convenient that you shifted from &quot;PoC and LGBTQ+&quot; to just LGBTQ+ the second you got called out on the PoC part. </div> </div> </div>The whole discussion went askew from the point you choose to interpret me saying that lots of the leftist talking points are more confined as &quot;these things are non-existent&quot;, which I didn't say, at all. I didn't even say I don't want these themes in the game, if you read my posts. I said I don't want these things framed in a certain narrative, which is entirelly different.<br /> <br /> Also yes, most of my friends there, or in West-European countries don't really encounter most of the culture war and are usually amused I do. And I mostly do, because I read rpg-related forums and pages, to be honest. And HEMA-related ones, to some extent. Somehow culture warriors from all sides love these.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this fails to see how things are complicated and interconnected. When, to keep on the example, young men of color are over-criminalized, it decreases their ability to economically contribute, putting more economic stress on WoC in those communities (hey, feminist stuff!) as they have to cover the same economic costs as other women who have more support from the men in their ethnic groups, which creates a vicious cycle of reduced wealth, opportunity, and stability leading to more criminal activity, leading to more over-policing, leading to more over-criminalization, repeat. This isn't a &quot;narrative&quot; this is a well studied fact. </div> </div> </div>Oh, the narrative, from either side, doesn't start here, but usually at &quot;why these young men are over-criminalized&quot; and &quot;how we should remedy this&quot; and after that everyone goes apeshit. Which is understandable, but doesn't help the problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you offer no proof besides the majority of the population simply not seeing it as a problem rather than anything to support it not being a problem with much broader impact than people acknowledge. </div> </div> </div>And you offer proof that it is? Honestly, I'm not here to write a sociological paper, or thesis on the topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right. You serious need to get out of your bubble, because you know jack shit about US politics other than whatever little section of commenters you listen to. </div> </div> </div>And just below, you act as if you know jackshit about Hungarian politics...<br /> <br /> And what &quot;commenters&quot; should I listen to? The ones you agree with? Regardless, the mentioned disconnect between the mentioned groups is patently evident even for me, an outsider and yes, self-acknowledged dabler. But by all means, keep doing the things you guys are doing, it looks like it's working well! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How long of a time could they have been digging this grave? </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Since the socialist era, at minimum. But it got worse since the regime change, I think, to the point, where &quot;liberal&quot; became a derogatory term, not among just the far-right, but among the general population outside their socio-cultural and geographical bubble.<br /> <br /> And just to mention it, I'm being usually labeled as a &quot;filthy liberal&quot;, even among my more right-leaning friends, with which I have frequent arguments over things like what Europe should do with the migrant crisis and even whether we should or should not have free university education, or supporting churches with general tax funds. Or government-funded gender studies courses on universities, to which I said &quot;yes&quot; even if I don't agree with a lot of things coming from those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm older than the Third Republic, and Orban's been PM for ~1/3 of it (and isn't the only right leaning PM Hungary's had since dropping Communism). </div> </div> </div>That's why you being an American comes through. Even the first Orb\u00e1n government was quite different than the post-2010 ones and the other &quot;right-leaning&quot; ones didn't have many commonalities with these either. The &quot;right&quot; and &quot;left&quot; dichotomy in the American sense just doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm fine with the rather left leaning approach of WtA's current status. </div> </div> </div>With the leaning, me too. As I said, I liked that WoD games were like that. I'm a rather anti-authoritarian person, with agreement with most of the moderate left's values. I just don1t want those things framed in a certain contemporary narrative, because to be honest, I'm getting fed up with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I explained my position in the rest of the paragraph so you didn't have to ask. </div> </div> </div>No, you didn't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You just said that the examples didn't differ and that the handling of these things were the same and I disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's your argumentation other than, &quot;I don't like to read them that way?&quot; </div> </div> </div>That they weren't written that way? Just like the Brujah contained leftist activist themes, but wasn't about that, primarily, the Traditions contained cultural stuff and yes, in some cases, were tied to ethnic groups, but wasn't focused on minority rights activism, especially not the kind we see today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) By necessity the Traditions all have minority rights activists in their numbers, because they all support groups that are minorities, even if no single Tradition is a universal minority right's activist group. </div> </div> </div>Same as above. Do the Brujah have neo-marxists (it's being just an example there) among their ranks? Yes. Are the Brujah a neo-marxist clan? No. Do the Traditions have minority rights activists? Yes. Are the tRaditions about minority rights activism? No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Traditions as a whole are explicitly a minority rights activist group by their founding principles. The Resolution of Intent directly committed all the member Traditions to mutual defense of each other and their cultural practices. </div> </div> </div>That's a very far-reaching take on minority rights activism. By that, churches are minority rights activist groups, by default.<br /> <br /> Most of them are minorities only in the sense of standing aside from the general population as mages, not in the sense &quot;minority&quot; is usually used. Okay, <i>some</i> of them could be viewed as religious minorities, in Western society, but it's more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> Are Werewolves a minority now? Changelings? Vampires?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The Traditions and the Disparate Alliance can both be so without contradiction. </div> </div> </div>Well, the Diparates are much more of a group arbitraritly put together from the smaller groups with strong ties to ethnic or sub-cultural groups. It does have a much stronger &quot;Minorities Assemble&quot; vibe than the more-encompassing Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like you're conflating things and misrepresenting Satyros there. </div> </div> </div>I said on a FB thread that the Prelude misrepresent and oversimplify the groups. He agreed. He even said, further on, that the Technocracy is both rightist <i>and </i>leftist authoritarian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are absolutely black and white issues in Mage, he's responsible for writing in a few of them. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Nephandi aaaaaaand... that's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And he also wrote a bunch of contemporary narratives into the game. </div> </div> </div>And mostly handled it with much more grace than I fear future books will. As I've said, I didn't feel M20 being overtly preachy. In books of secrets, he let his personal oppinions and beliefs coming through more directly, in the FAQ, but mostly, he and the old WW writers (or even most of the OPP writers) handled the portrayal of things in a way I was satisfied with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to twist the black and white stuff to fit contemporary narratives (like &quot;Trump supporters are all Nephandi or Nephandi dupes!&quot;) is clearly not good, but there's two different issues here. </div> </div> </div>No, that's exactly the same issue. Oversimplified and misrepresenting writing to pander to a group's real-world narrative and tastes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, and we're really not in any danger of that happening any time soon... so seems weird to worry about it for W5. </div> </div> </div>We have a different perception on this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have seven Tribes focused on human minorities, </div> </div> </div>Right there. &quot;Hailing from&quot;, or &quot;connected to&quot; is not the same as &quot;focused on&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> another Tribe focused on a historically mistreated ethnic group that was in the middle of a major struggle when first developed, and another Tribe focused on persecution of animals... so 9/13 of the Tribes have this as something they're fighting against, plus the remaining four (and the other half of the Fianna being a borderline case in the first group) all still have this as a theme going in the opposite direction (ex: the Fenrir and sexism). They game has always had this as one (yes not the only) central thematic elements. </div> </div> </div>Yes, these things were present, but were primary, honestly, only in the case of the Wendigo and Uktena, being an American game and all that. The others were secondary and tertiary themes, with the possible exception of the Gnawers very strong time to the lowest strata of society and those fallen out of it.<br /> <br /> Even then, how the game presents and discusses these themes weren't framed in a too-biased way, in my eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Capitalism is explicitly a Weaver element, and only wholly embraced by... the Glass Walkers because they're the pro-Weaver Tribe. None of the other Tribes &quot;happily&quot; participate in capitalism, they just don't have much of a choice if they're going to participate in mainstream human society (which a good number of them don't advocate doing much of anyway). </div> </div> </div>I bet the Shadow Lords aren't too much against it either. The others, yeah, they recognize the need, but they are not human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Silver Fangs especially aren't capitalists, because that takes power away from royalty, as well as capitalism not being a system that rewards merit, but rewards pre-existing economic advantages earned or unearned. </div> </div> </div>Riiiiiight, okay won't go down this rabbit hole. I'm totally not a &quot;the market solves everything&quot; type of guy, but still, that's a pretty biased and narrow view on it, but I'm not suprised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus all the stuff Saur Ops beat me to. </div> </div> </div>Answered there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh. WtA has a lot of themes, but the whole &quot;Captain Planet&quot; criticism is based on how little it explores most of them for the culture warrior eco-terrorists fighting capitalism its military industrial complex to be the dominant narrative of the game anyway. </div> </div> </div>As I've said, I have a degree in part because of it. The environmentalist theme and the animistic-spiritualist stuff and playing murderous furballs always were the centric themes of the game for me, not minority rights activism. If other people focus on that, because that is what interests them, that's fine by me, but I don1t want the game to be entirely focused on that and again, I don1t want the game to follow a contemporary political and ideological narrative slavishly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the whole problem with the WoD (at least pre-V5 and we'll see how that goes) is that the End Times Are Nigh, which makes a lot of the themes irrelevant because they'd take too long to explore in-game before the Apocalypse happens unless you ignore that in your personal games. </div> </div> </div>That's more of a Revised thing, IMO and even then, the Revised games explored a lot of them. Just, you know, not everyone played/is playing these games as social justice activism simulators, focusing instead on other themes, or even on the same themes, but from a different perspective.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-04-2018, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:13:48-07:00","id":1251458,"title":"","content":"And that is what I had energy and time for a while. It took me more than 3 hours, after work and I think I've had enough. These long and honestly, pointless arguments, which inevitably spiral down to ideological mud-flinging just tires me out. Everyone, I wish you fun from here on, with any style and themes you want to play with and focus on this and other (WoD or not) games! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> M\u00e1rk departs the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-04-2018, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T17:38:45-07:00","id":1251796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251451#post1251451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, no, the Wendigo are not racist. They don't control the systemic means of oppression, so it'd be really, really difficult to be that way. <b>They don't like white people,</b> sure, but there's just cause for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pssss. Hey. Over here. <br /> <br /> That's...uh...that's RACISM.<br /> <br /> It's not systemic racism, sure. But it is 100% most definitely racist. We don't have to agree, by the way. I'm just going by the literal interpretation of the definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T03:15:33-07:00","id":1251873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251796#post1251796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pssss. Hey. Over here. <br /> <br /> That's...uh...that's RACISM.<br /> <br /> It's not systemic racism, sure. But it is 100% most definitely racist. We don't have to agree, by the way. I'm just going by the literal interpretation of the definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what definition you're using however. I think that the common usage definition is very useful for interactions between individuals (i.e. that group of garou were really racist, almost killed my kin because he is white) but is a poor model when it comes to interaction between groups. When you're looking at something as wide as a totem or a tribe, prejudiced is a better descriptor.<br /> <br /> Then again this is an argument of semantics, and we're all on the same page as to whether disliking someone over skin colour is wrong, it's more an issue of what we call that. As for any groups of Garou or even spirits with an intense prejudice against white people, there is historical cause for this within IRL and setting history/politics. So calling the prejudice of a historically oppressed group, or a group which has been *harmed* by racism &quot;racism&quot; feels like a gross oversimplification. Native Americans or aboriginal peoples etc. with a profound dislike for white people aren't akin to white people with a prejudice going in the other direction. One is the hatred of a marginalized group against their former/current oppressors, one is part of a tradition of genocide and supremacy. Neither is good, but we should have different words for them in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I'd say that what you're saying here is correct in terms of what you'd teach high schoolers; broadly the right idea, but lacking nuance. People who spend all of their time studying this stuff (or talk to people who do and read their work) come to more refined conclusions, as with any subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-06-2018, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T06:20:01-07:00","id":1251898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251873#post1251873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling the prejudice of a historically oppressed group, or a group which has been *harmed* by racism &quot;racism&quot; feels like a gross oversimplification. Native Americans or aboriginal peoples etc. with a profound dislike for white people aren't akin to white people with a prejudice going in the other direction. One is the hatred of a marginalized group against their former/current oppressors, one is part of a tradition of genocide and supremacy. Neither is good, but we should have different words for them in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I'd say that what you're saying here is correct in terms of what you'd teach high schoolers; broadly the right idea, but lacking nuance. People who spend all of their time studying this stuff (or talk to people who do and read their work) come to more refined conclusions, as with any subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet if feels much more of a gross oversymplification to call it *prejudice*. While racism it's a very specific word, prejudice it's much more ample and hasn't the same negative connotations: I can be prejudiced if I decide I don't like tomato before tasting it, that's hardly the same feeling as the hatred native american may feel for the white, don't you think?.<br /> <br /> Since calling the prejudice of a historically oppressed group, or a group which has been *harmed* by racism &quot;racism&quot; feels like a gross oversimplification, the correct and nuanced approach to define the prejudice against (or from) a historically oppressed group it's not to co-opt a word that has a common usage (racism, which means to hate someone because of his race) but rather to define a technical therm (like, say, intitucionalized racism for racism that it's ingrained in the building blocks of society).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-06-2018, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T07:27:35-07:00","id":1251910,"title":"","content":"Racism is a real thing, and for fictional beings, that value ancestry and blood lineage and ethnicity it is totally okay to be racist, to a certain degree. It is to some degree okay to say &quot;we don't want anything to do with those people&quot; before becoming too isolationistic or paranoid. As a game element, it is okay that racism exists and that certain tribes are described as being more racist, or sexist than others, and some as being hypocrites about it.<br /> <br /> I, too, find it sad, that inherent conflict and tension within the game world is reduced by inserting what feels like forced political correctness. Males with the Black Furies, non-native american Wendigo and so on - if depicted as &quot;normal&quot;. Im not saying, a afro-american person can't have a garou child which on the other partners side has pure Get of Fenris ancestry. But, much like Evan-Heals-the-Past, such a person would have to fight against preconceptions.<br /> <br /> Tribes, in WtA, are literal tribes for the most part, that means biological and cultural entities, that are defined by attributes it's members share. They aren't like the 'tribes' in 'Lord of the Flies' - made-up off members that not necessarily share biological traits.<br /> For that, I found it unfortunate, that tribes remain as a term in WtF, because the tribes in Forsaken are too, more like clubs or interest groups or camps.<br /> <br /> That said, WtA characters, in the past edition, had a society with a lot of inherent flaws. Rewriting them today is kind of like rewriting history. One could argue, that the tribes should have evolved and become better than this, but this realistic. Society doesn't change like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:52:54-07:00","id":1251939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1251796#post1251796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pssss. Hey. Over here.<br /> <br /> That's...uh...that's RACISM.<br /> <br /> It's not systemic racism, sure. But it is 100% most definitely racist. We don't have to agree, by the way. I'm just going by the literal interpretation of the definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Wendigo label all others as &quot;lesser races&quot; and have a bizarre, twisted reading of early human classifications based on the four humors, and they want to exterminate everyone else, I'll worry. In the meantime, they have a very reasonable sense of resentment and distrust toward colonial holdouts who want to keep colonizing (i.e. killing off indigenous people and culturally assimilating anyone left so that they can declare vast swaths of people who were there before &quot;extinct&quot;).<br /> <br /> Also, going off on a tangent about the tribe's attitude as often presented, they shouldn't be written as valuing any kind of native blood quantum, because that's something that started with US and Canadian efforts to dictate who counted as indigenous. That seems like it would be a rather strange idea to ascribe to the Wendigo, especially since PB got disconnected from human ethnic groups in W20. Arguably, it wasn't even all that strong of a connection to begin with if Evan Heals the Past had 2 dots of it. In fact, the three Wendigo of mixed ancestry statted up in Warriors of the Apocalypse (Evan and the Kachina twins) all had it at two dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T01:27:08-07:00","id":1252146,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed is not solely biological. It describes how close the character is to being an ideal paragon of the tribe, so there are mystical and mental aspects to it. One has to share a certain mind set and certain ideas to be a member of a tribe, just as much as one is expected to have certain hereditary biological traits. In addition there are mystic aspects like connection to ancestors of the tribe or spirits of the tribal totems brood.<br /> <br /> y guess is, if one is trying to convince a sept to be allowed to perform a Rite of Passage for entering into their tribe, and perform well, so that the tribe members and the totem spirit are convinced it is necessary to show all aspects to a degree. And if one lacks the one aspect (in Evan's case the telltale biological traits), the other ones could compensate (in Evan's case the mindset and connection to Ancestors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-07-2018, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T09:41:06-07:00","id":1253621,"title":"","content":"So, sjw staff aside. How do you think White Wolf will deal with new info being floating around, like forests expanding exponentially, wildlife returning to Europe and moving into cities, basically an invasion of new hybrids, runaway biomodded lifeforms and wildlife moving into cities? as well as plastic being not as toxic as thought, Age of Crystals caused by humans and other drastic changes to both opinion and actual ecosystem not anticipated by WtA. <br /> <br /> Seems like Wyld gaining an upper hand and starting to subsume Weaver if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T10:07:57-07:00","id":1253633,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'd call &quot;forests expanding exponentially&quot; a thing to worry about for the game. We're seeing the efforts of sustained replanting of forests in wealthy nations for years in carefully managed fashion; not some massive explosion in natural tree growth. And while reforestation is outpacing deforestation (again though, there's human pressure towards this), not all forests are created equally. Expansion of sustainable tree farming operations increases the total forest cover, but isn't the same ecological impact as an old growth forest or tropical rain forest.<br /> <br /> Wildlife coming into the cities isn't anything new, even if some species have discovered city living isn't so bad more recently than others.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Given the conceits of the World of Darkness meaning these efforts probably aren't as effective and/or benign as in the real world, and how human controlled this all this, I'd say there's little need to worry about the idea that the Wyld is in trouble.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T23:02:10-07:00","id":1253813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1253633#post1253633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd call &quot;forests expanding exponentially&quot; a thing to worry about for the game. We're seeing the efforts of sustained replanting of forests in wealthy nations for years in carefully managed fashion; not some massive explosion in natural tree growth. And while reforestation is outpacing deforestation (again though, there's human pressure towards this), not all forests are created equally. Expansion of sustainable tree farming operations increases the total forest cover, but isn't the same ecological impact as an old growth forest or tropical rain forest.<br /> <br /> Wildlife coming into the cities isn't anything new, even if some species have discovered city living isn't so bad more recently than others.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Given the conceits of the World of Darkness meaning these efforts probably aren't as effective and/or benign as in the real world, and how human controlled this all this, I'd say there's little need to worry about the idea that the Wyld is in trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually tree growth rate has increased due to more carbon in the atmosphere. agriculture runoffs also contribute, mainly to water plants (not always good).<br /> <br /> Taking into account the premise of WtA premise being based on apocalyptic environmentalist predictions of 20th century it makes sense to modify the situation somewhat. You don't need to make it all unicorns and rainbows, to keep the mood. I would depict it as Wyld finally gaining an advantage, but creating new dangers out of it, like uncontrollably spawning hybrids and mutants, invasive species, bizzare new spirits. can throw in greater wyld spirit involvement with humans and tech, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 09-13-2018, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T23:37:04-07:00","id":1253817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1253813#post1253813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually tree growth rate has increased due to more carbon in the atmosphere. agriculture runoffs also contribute, mainly to water plants (not always good).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is some of this. Though carbon in the atmosphere is causing more growth via warming increasing tree habitats in places not traditionally used for lumber (higher tree lines on mountains, melting permafrost allowing forests to expand farther north).<br /> <br /> However, this is unsustainable in the long run. Human intervention by planting is vastly more responsible than anything else.<br /> <br /> Ireland, has, for example, increased it's forest cover ten times what it was when they started a program of reforestation. That's vastly more trees because of a government program to plant them, than any other factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Taking into account the premise of WtA premise being based on apocalyptic environmentalist predictions of 20th century it makes sense to modify the situation somewhat. </div> </div> </div>Climate change is still a huge problem that's already reached the point where it is going to get worse before it gets better no matter what we do. More trees and plastic not being toxic but still causing lots of problems doesn't paint a rosy picture for the future of our climate. We're still dealing with species extinctions, unsustainable resource management, habitat destruction.... The predictions are still pretty bad if humanity doesn't do something soon.<br /> <br /> Modify? Sure. But the &quot;apocalyptic&quot; predictions are still basically on point for where things are headed.<br /> <br /> If anything things are even more suited for WtA's premise now. Climate change refugees, the social instability inherent in that being a thing, and the exploitation of these situations, are pretty nasty things. There's a reason most countries consider climate change a national security issue: there's direct links between climate change induced social instability, and increased militant group activity (obviously climate change doesn't cause these groups to exist, it just provides them a more favorable condition to grow in power). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would depict it as Wyld finally gaining an advantage,.. </div> </div> </div>The problem is &quot;chaos&quot; isn't really gaining an advantage in all this. The Wyld might be 'striking back' but it's just driving humanity farther into the arms of the Weaver for security, or the Wyrm for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T14:16:02-07:00","id":1254328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1253817#post1253817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. There is some of this. Though carbon in the atmosphere is causing more growth via warming increasing tree habitats in places not traditionally used for lumber (higher tree lines on mountains, melting permafrost allowing forests to expand farther north).<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Climate change is still a huge problem that's already reached the point where it is going to get worse before it gets better no matter what we do. More trees and plastic not being toxic but still causing lots of problems doesn't paint a rosy picture for the future of our climate. We're still dealing with species extinctions, unsustainable resource management, habitat destruction.... The predictions are still pretty bad if humanity doesn't do something soon.<br /> <br /> 3. If anything things are even more suited for WtA's premise now. Climate change refugees, the social instability inherent in that being a thing, and the exploitation of these situations, are pretty nasty things.<br /> <br /> 4. There's a reason most countries consider climate change a national security issue: there's direct links between climate change induced social instability, and increased militant group activity (obviously climate change doesn't cause these groups to exist, it just provides them a more favorable condition to grow in power).<br /> <br /> 5. The problem is &quot;chaos&quot; isn't really gaining an advantage in all this. The Wyld might be 'striking back' but it's just driving humanity farther into the arms of the Weaver for security, or the Wyrm for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I will believe professional scientists over you, sorry. <br /> 2. Not as much, and not as humancentric as we thought. <br /> 3. It matters because? WtA centers planet, not humans (go to Mage for that). Compared to past there is an improvement anyway in such humanitarian matters.<br /> 4. Again. migrations and conflicts caused by climate (droughts, floods) is nothing new and is managed better then ever. <br /> 5. in that case we have drastically different understandings of 'Chaos'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T16:21:26-07:00","id":1254346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1254328#post1254328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I will believe professional scientists over you, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to go there, start citing some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Not as much, and not as humancentric as we thought. </div> </div> </div>This sounds like the &quot;professional scientists&quot; you're going to cite are those mysterious &quot;3%&quot; of scientists that claim anthropogenic sources of climate change don't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. It matters because? WtA centers planet, not humans (go to Mage for that). </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. Humans have always been central to WtA because humans are at the center of the fight over the future of our planet. Human born werewolves are the most numerous ones, which is why the Tribes are so dominated by human-centric ethnic concerns and social issues.<br /> <br /> I don't need to &quot;go to Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compared to past there is an improvement anyway in such humanitarian matters. </div> </div> </div>Again, citation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Again. migrations and conflicts caused by climate (droughts, floods) is nothing new and is managed better then ever. </div> </div> </div>They are worse than ever, and even if management solutions have improved, they're being taxed beyond their limits as the numbers grow beyond funding and similar allocations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. in that case we have drastically different understandings of 'Chaos'. </div> </div> </div>Probably, but I don't see how it comments on the point that Weaver based solutions overpowering the Wyld is at all a symbol of the Wyld resurgence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T07:18:51-07:00","id":1254496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1253621#post1253621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, sjw staff aside. How do you think White Wolf will deal with new info being floating around, like forests expanding exponentially, wildlife returning to Europe and moving into cities, basically an invasion of new hybrids, runaway biomodded lifeforms and wildlife moving into cities? as well as plastic being not as toxic as thought, Age of Crystals caused by humans and other drastic changes to both opinion and actual ecosystem not anticipated by WtA.<br /> <br /> Seems like Wyld gaining an upper hand and starting to subsume Weaver if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the WoD, large portions of forests and other wilderness never ended up being harvested or settled because they were spooky and humans were reeling from the Impergium, and the Wyld was still assumed to be on the back foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T10:46:56-07:00","id":1254557,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, I'm interested to see how character creation changes. My bet is they will follow the same basic model from V5, with simplified skill list and selection. I've heard a few folks mention that the Hunger mechanic will be mirrored by a Rage mechanic (and the Animalism discipline outright mentions being able to sense and reduce or induce Frenzy or Rage with capital first letters). I'd imagine that rather than a &quot;Predator type&quot; we'd see some equivalent to the Auspice of the character, to reflect how they approach their devotion to Gaia and the fight against the Wyrm. Tribe will take the place of Clan would be my next guess. My biggest area of questioning is what will be the new Gifts. Will there be a simplfying of the Gift list, or perhaps organizing them based on the spirit types that give them with tribes &amp; auspices having affinities for certain spirits perhaps? Another food for thought: will the Breed give skill bonuses to reflect upbringing? how will it be manifested? Will there be Gnosis, or will there be a soothing of Rage in place of Gnosis as a separate resource, as Rage and spiritual peace would be a form of balancing act?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T11:44:40-07:00","id":1254806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1254346#post1254346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to go there, start citing some.<br /> <br /> This sounds like the &quot;professional scientists&quot; you're going to cite are those mysterious &quot;3%&quot; of scientists that claim anthropogenic sources of climate change don't matter.<br /> <br /> Bullshit. Humans have always been central to WtA because humans are at the center of the fight over the future of our planet. Human born werewolves are the most numerous ones, which is why the Tribes are so dominated by human-centric ethnic concerns and social issues.<br /> <br /> I don't need to &quot;go to Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, citation.<br /> <br /> They are worse than ever, and even if management solutions have improved, they're being taxed beyond their limits as the numbers grow beyond funding and similar allocations.<br /> <br /> Probably, but I don't see how it comments on the point that Weaver based solutions overpowering the Wyld is at all a symbol of the Wyld resurgence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://wattsupwiththat.com/2018/08/03/twelve-invisible-eco-catastrophes-and-threats-of-doom-that-are-actually-fake/\" target=\"_blank\">https://wattsupwiththat.com/2018/08/...actually-fake/</a><br /> <br /> Not &quot;don't matter&quot;, but &quot;are one of several&quot; including sun activity, cycles of heating/cooling, etc.<br /> <br /> They became central in last half a millennium max. and in the end it's the planet/Gaia at the center stage. If you need Humans as the center of cosmos, not just a powerful species, you need to &quot;go to mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\":///assets/client/images/okr-logo-xs.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141\" target=\"_blank\"> Open Knowledge Repository </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141\" target=\"_blank\"> https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://stevenpinker.com/publications/enlightenment-now-case-reason-science-humanism-and-progress\" target=\"_blank\">https://stevenpinker.com/publication...m-and-progress</a><br /> <br /> Yeaah, in the past they just died. or invaded neighbors and killed/enslaved them. Don't compare situation to unattainable ideal, compare to IRL past, a very unpleasant one.<br /> <br /> Weaver based? How is uncontrolled, explosive chaos 'weaver'? How is explosive development of new species, minerals, modes of thought considered 'weaver'? New species of drug resistant bacteria, yearly virus waves, new hybrid plants and animals transported through freight carriers, genemodded/mutated species let loose wild and thriving, new &quot;age of crystals&quot; brought through human activity. <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't misunderstand me and get hackles up. I'm not saying there are no problems whatsoever, I'm saying situation is not nearly as apocalyptic and far different then seen in 1990-2000 when the main mood of the game was developed. Same thing happened with Technocracy, which was reworked in new editions. Instead of doubling down on the same old things I would prefer a refreshed approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 09-16-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T13:57:18-07:00","id":1254839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1254806#post1254806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://wattsupwiththat.com/2018/08/03/twelve-invisible-eco-catastrophes-and-threats-of-doom-that-are-actually-fake/\" target=\"_blank\">https://wattsupwiththat.com/2018/08/...actually-fake/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So... a bunch of non-scientific arguments with no data to back them up, by a guy that sold out to energy companies because trying to do real science to by up his claims didn't pan out of him.<br /> <br /> Seems like my, &quot;This sounds like the &quot;professional scientists&quot; you're going to cite are those mysterious &quot;3%&quot; of scientists that claim anthropogenic sources of climate change don't matter.&quot; prediction was spot on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not &quot;don't matter&quot;, but &quot;are one of several&quot; including sun activity, cycles of heating/cooling, etc. </div> </div> </div>You do realize that things like that - on the scale of change we're looking at - usually take longer to cycle than human civilization has existed?<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure, we're currently a blip on the geological time scale, and what's disastrous to us is nothing to the course of life on Earth over the long haul.<br /> <br /> That's no reason to kill ourselves and thousands of other species when we don't have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They became central in last half a millennium max. </div> </div> </div>Um... duh? Humans didn't have the technology and population to cause the level of impact we're causing now until recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and in the end it's the planet/Gaia at the center stage. </div> </div> </div>So... why is Gaia always in the background of the games? I mean, Gaia literally exists in WtA. But you can never talk directly to her. It's an epic quest just to try to get an audience with one of her high level avatars. If you're lucky you might meet a Kami that might have heard Gaia's voice once.<br /> <br /> Gaia isn't center stage, because the fate of planet is what the fight is over, not what the fight entails. Humanity has always been front and center in the books as the main arena of the fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you need Humans as the center of cosmos, not just a powerful species, you need to &quot;go to mage&quot;. </div> </div> </div>You need to consider shopping somewhere other than Strawman Barn for your arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141\" target=\"_blank\">https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/25141</a> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a report stating that we need to do <b>more</b> about global poverty, not that things are going great. To quote the foreward:<br /> <br /> &quot;I am confident that this report will go down as a major work of scholarship in an area of urgent global concern. The World Bank Group staff and I thank Tony and the Commission for their thoughtful analyses and recommendations. I would like to hope that they will be instrumental in improving our understanding of the extent of poverty and in making progress toward the goals of ending extreme poverty and promoting shared prosperity.&quot;<br /> <br /> You notice the lack of, &quot;Yay, we solved it!&quot; there?<br /> <br /> Also, this is a report on how to monitor poverty, it doesn't really make many final determinations on things like how to handle climate refugees besides the basic logic that decreasing individual poverty and community insolvency makes people more resilient to change and other communities more capable of absorbing populations that have to move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://stevenpinker.com/publications/enlightenment-now-case-reason-science-humanism-and-progress\" target=\"_blank\">https://stevenpinker.com/publication...m-and-progress</a> </div> </div> </div>Pinker is a cognitive scientist, not a climatologist (at least you cited a physicist and some economists before). While his goal of trying to get people to be realists over falling for sensationalism is noble, that doesn't mean there aren't big problems. He's also extremely prone to being extremely Eurocentric in his selection of data (things look really rosy when you ignore how you can't just export European liberal democracy to the world and suddenly everything will look like the EU's top 10 countries), and horrible at accepting negating factors to his points if they buck his promotion of the Enlightenment esp. when it comes to how flawed much of the Enlightenment was (he supports the idea that there is a genetic sex based difference in STEM performance with zero regard to centuries of women being excluded from participation in such pursuits).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's good to have people out there going, &quot;Hey, it's not all doom and gloom, there's hope, there's good, we need to fight for that instead of fighting each other.&quot; That doesn't mean you get to jump all the way to, &quot;global deaths from natural disasters are on the decline, so there's no need to rebuild Puerto Rico's infrastructure or obey mandatory evacuation orders, hurricanes just aren't as big of a problem any more!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also... Pinker's a Technocrat mouth piece if there ever was one... so go to Mage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeaah, in the past they just died. or invaded neighbors and killed/enslaved them. </div> </div> </div>We're still doing all these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't compare situation to unattainable ideal, compare to IRL past, a very unpleasant one. </div> </div> </div>Wtf are you even talking about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weaver based? </div> </div> </div>Reforestation and reintroduction efforts, environmental legislation, pretty much everything Pinker talks about as the net positivities of civilization and the way technology and rational thought will save us, etc. That's all Weaver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is uncontrolled, explosive chaos 'weaver'? </div> </div> </div>What significant uncontrolled and explosive chaos are we talking about? Most of the chaos world wide is either humans mucking things up with irresponsible use of Weaver tech (yay drug resistant diseases evolving rapidly!), or more Wyrm than Wyld in application (nothing new or really all that chaotic about a tornado in the grand scheme, but they sure are destructive).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is explosive development of new species, minerals, modes of thought considered 'weaver'? </div> </div> </div>Well, when the developments of new species are driven by technology instead of nature... that's what we call Weaver in WtA. Sorry, but that's just proving my point.<br /> <br /> Discovering new things is pretty neutral. A mineral sitting around in a cave for a few million years that humans just discovered isn't an explosive bit of anything. There are a bunch of new minerals... that are oh wait the product of technology again, not nature randomly and chaotically forming brand new ones out of the blue.<br /> <br /> Modes of thought? How do you even propose to measure the rate of development of mode of thought? How are we not still solidly in Weaver territory here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> New species of drug resistant bacteria, yearly virus waves, new hybrid plants and animals transported through freight carriers, genemodded/mutated species let loose wild and thriving, new &quot;age of crystals&quot; brought through human activity. </div> </div> </div>Right... &quot;human activity&quot; aka technology, aka the Weaver, not the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Also, 99% of this is just organisms doing what they've always done, but with extra inputs. It's like claiming that North American wolves discovering sheep when Europeans introduced them as a viable food source represents some major change in nature. It doesn't. Bacteria have been in a war against antibacterial compounds since before animals evolved (there's a reason plants are the origin of antibiotics and researches are still phyto-mining in hopes of finding new ones). Some viruses have been using cyclical wave propagation as far back as we can study because it's a reliable infection pattern with animals. Plants hybridize all the time, it's basically an essential aspect of 'plant' beyond the basic definition of the Kingdom, there isn't an explosion in plant hybrids (besides purposefully made human ones anyway) there's just an explosion in people genetically testing plants to realize they're dealing with more hybrids than individual species.<br /> <br /> And invasive species is definitely explosively happening now (though again, because of humans, not the Wyld) and it's horrible for the environment. Zebra mussels might be thriving... that doesn't mean it's a good thing for the Great Lakes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't misunderstand me and get hackles up. </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to get my hackles up:<br /> <br /> 1) Learn how to cite scientists better.<br /> <br /> 2) Don't make an argument that is basically, &quot;there's no reason to worry about climate change disasters because the Technocracy will fix it all and got to Mage for disagreeing with me!&quot; bull shit.<br /> <br /> 3) Don't cite shills for the energy corporations, or people that think that the earlier Enlightenment's sexism is justified, as reasons for why things aren't so bad. The fact that people like these aren't considered quacks is part of the problem even if they talk a good talk.<br /> <br /> 4) Don't tell me to &quot;got to Mage&quot; because you don't have a leg to stand on regarding the themes of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> 5) Stop using human technological impacts on the environment as justification of a Wyld resurgence<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying there are no problems whatsoever, I'm saying situation is not nearly as apocalyptic and far different then seen in 1990-2000 when the main mood of the game was developed. </div> </div> </div>The way you're making this argument is effectively the same thing.<br /> <br /> You're basically say that if an average of five less people die per capita from gun violence this year than last year, that gun violence is still a problem, but it's not one that actually matters and we can ignore of something else.<br /> <br /> That's not how reality works, and that's not how a game that focuses on a real world issue should work. The climate change models are still <b>horrible</b> without change. Will life go on? In the real world sure. In WtA? That level of destruction is a fail condition because it means the Wyrm wins. WtA has a spirit of corruption that we don't have to consider IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same thing happened with Technocracy, which was reworked in new editions. </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is a faction of mages, not a fundamental theme of the game. And the change is more in adding nuance to the Technocracy to leave room to play it, rather than really changing the core of its narrative role.<br /> <br /> And something that has been part of WtA from the get go? The Garou suck at nuance. A key part of the game is that they're fighting something far more nuanced than they're really equipped for (largely because of their ancestors' past failings). The Garou are mostly hammers seeing everything as nails, in a world that needs someone to build an Erector set, with minority of them desperately trying to make the rest see things more clearly.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to dump that. That still matters... that matters for the reasons some of the people you cite would agree with! The Garou are not good environmentalists, they're reactionary terrorists (from a human perspective) that want to be good environmentalists but don't know how as a society. WtA has always had an element of highlighting both the need to protect the environement, and an element that the Garou go too far when we consider how to reflect this in our own lives.<br /> <br /> &quot;Refreshing&quot; the approach misses the whole damned point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T03:59:16-07:00","id":1255459,"title":"","content":"Changing the subject a bit, and going by the alterations to the meta made by V5, how much do you want to bet that they'll kill King Albrecht in the new edition and make the Shadow Lords the new Alpha Tribe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T06:38:08-07:00","id":1255471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1249810-werewolf-5th-concerns?p=1255459#post1255459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the subject a bit, and going by the alterations to the meta made by V5, how much do you want to bet that they'll kill King Albrecht in the new edition and make the Shadow Lords the new Alpha Tribe?</div> </div> </div> </di